%20v7.4.html","Complete game code, styles, interface, and Canvas graphics are contained in this HTML file.",[1146],{"_841":1147,"_809":340,"_870":1148},"Play Pirate Fleet Commander","Use WASD or the arrow keys to sail and the on-screen controls for fleet management. Desktop recommended.",[1150],{"_841":1042,"_809":1029,"_870":-7},[1152,1153,1154,1155],"Play the fleet game and test sailing, combat, repairs, and upgrades.","Read the author’s collection-wide AI disclosure.","Inspect the individual HTML file’s game loop and fleet economy.","Download that file and change one ship statistic before replaying.","Joey Salmons says the collection began with Gemini 2.5 Pro in AI Studio and Claude Sonnet 4.5, with manual edits limited to small balance changes. The exact model used for this version is not specified.",[1152,1153,1154,1155],{"_841":1042,"_809":1029,"_802":891},{"_841":1147,"_809":340,"_802":974,"_870":1148},{"_841":1142,"_809":1143,"_870":1144,"_932":933},{"_841":1028,"_809":1029,"_870":1139},[],"example:beach-kitty-ai-campaign","Beach Kitty","A cat-led Phaser campaign that combines running, platforming, shooting, and other arcade mechanics, with optional generated cat art.","/examples/beach-kitty-ai-campaign/",{"_804":125,"_805":1164,"_807":1165,"_920":1222,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":1221,"_901":1223,"_892":1224,"_881":1225,"_816":1226,"_867":1227,"_857":1228},[1169,1170,1171,1172,1173,1174,1175,1176,1177,1178,1179,1180,1181,1182,1183,1184,1185,1186,1187],{"_837":805,"_843":1164,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":1165,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1222,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":1221,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":1216,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":1212,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":1207,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":1202,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":1197,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":1191,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":1189},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":346,"_191":1188,"_193":345,"_816":344,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":200},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/beach-kitty-ai-campaign.webp",[1190,1022],"Claude Code",[1192,1193],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":1194,"_809":1195},"Phaser · First Game Guide","/resources/phaser/","/resources/claude-code/",[1198],{"_841":1199,"_809":1200,"_870":1201},"See the author’s tool attribution","https://github.com/matthewod11-stack/CatRunner#built-with","The README names Claude Code and Gemini and distinguishes the playable campaign from its optional generation features.",[1203],{"_841":1204,"_809":1205,"_870":1206},"Open the complete campaign project","https://github.com/matthewod11-stack/CatRunner","Complete Phaser and React project with scenes, systems, assets, audio, API routes, and build configuration. Gemini is optional for the core game.",[1208],{"_841":1209,"_809":344,"_870":1210},"Play Beach Kitty","Keyboard and touch controls are available. Early runner controls include Space or Up to jump, Down to duck, and P or Escape to pause.","build log",[1213],{"_841":1214,"_809":1215,"_870":-7},"Read the development progress log","https://github.com/matthewod11-stack/CatRunner/blob/main/PROGRESS.md",[1217,1218,1219,1220],"Play the campaign and compare how its scenes share one cat character.","Read the progress log alongside the author’s Claude Code and Gemini disclosure.","Inspect the Phaser scenes and React shell to understand their responsibilities.","Run npm install and npm run dev; 