 and UI assignments.","Compare the shared state and event contract with each teammate’s completed module.","Review the coordination notes to see how parallel work was assigned and integrated.","The author documents a Claude Opus 4.6 agent team, shared scaffolding, separate file ownership, and the exact prompts assigned to each teammate.",[3356,3357,3358,3359],{"_841":3353,"_809":3354,"_802":1230},{"_841":3349,"_809":228,"_802":974,"_870":3350},{"_841":1913,"_809":3345,"_870":3346,"_932":933},{"_841":3340,"_809":3341,"_870":3342},[694,1993],"example:tron-exonix-claude","TRON: EXONIX","A neon 3D territory-capture game built through Claude Code, Godot MCP, Blender MCP, and generated assets, with human design and playtest feedback.","/examples/tron-exonix-claude/",{"_804":175,"_805":3368,"_807":3369,"_920":3433,"_2871":3434,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":3427,"_901":3435,"_892":3436,"_881":3437,"_816":3438,"_867":3439,"_857":3440},[3373,3374,3375,3376,3377,3378,3379,3380,3381,3382,3383,3384,3385,3386,3387,3388,3389,3390,3391,3392],{"_837":805,"_843":3368,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3369,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3433,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":3428,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3427,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3422,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3418,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":892,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3414,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3409,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3404,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3395,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3394},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":231,"_191":3393,"_193":230,"_816":232,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":200},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/tron-exonix-claude.webp",[1190],[3396,3397,3398,3399],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":1448,"_809":1449},{"_841":3402,"_809":3403},{"_841":3400,"_809":3401},"MCP for Blender","/resources/mcp-for-blender/","Godot MCP · Coding-Solo","/resources/godot-mcp/",[3405],{"_841":3406,"_809":3407,"_870":3408},"Read how the agent workflow was assembled","https://github.com/witnesstodark/tron-exonix/blob/master/CLAUDE.md","The creator’s reproducible setup record explains the AI’s implementation work, human material review, generation tools, and local launch requirements.",[3410],{"_841":3411,"_809":3412,"_870":3413},"Open the complete Godot game project","https://github.com/witnesstodark/tron-exonix","Includes the Godot project, scripts, shaders, models, textures, audio, and generation scripts. Local play requires Godot 4.7 standard; API access is only needed to regenerate assets.",[3415],{"_841":3416,"_809":232,"_870":3417},"Play TRON: EXONIX","Creator-hosted Godot web build. Click to enter the grid, press Space to deploy, use the arrow keys to move, and Escape for the menu. A keyboard and a WebGL-capable browser are recommended.",[3419],{"_841":3420,"_809":3421,"_870":-7},"Follow the creator’s complete workflow","https://www.top3d.ai/learn/claude-godot-mcp-3d-game",[3423,3424,3425,3426],"Play the web build and study territory capture, trail hazards, enemy movement, and sector progression.","Follow the creator’s tutorial from prototype through materials, audio, effects, and web export.","Read CLAUDE.md to understand the agent, Godot MCP, Blender review, and asset-generation workflow.","Open game/project.godot in Godot 4.7 and press F5; study the scripts alongside the included models, textures, and audio.","The creator documents Claude writing gameplay, shaders, VFX, and UI while a human steers mechanics and materials. The repository includes the actual Godot game, generated assets, and the asset-generation scripts.",[2843,3429,3430,2872,3431,3432],"Nano Banana","PATINA","Stable Audio","ElevenLabs","Godot 4.7 · GDScript",[2843,3429,3430,2872,3431,3432],[3423,3424,3425,3426],{"_841":3420,"_809":3421,"_802":892},{"_841":3416,"_809":232,"_802":974,"_870":3417},{"_841":3411,"_809":3412,"_932":933,"_870":3413},{"_841":3406,"_809":3407,"_870":3408},[694,1481,3441,3442],"godot-mcp","mcp-for-blender","example:moonlight-mayhem-codex","Moonlight & Mayhem","A 3D museum heist made with Codex: rescue two raccoon crewmates, evade security, stack the crew, and steal the Golden Sardine.","/examples/moonlight-mayhem-codex/",{"_804":173,"_805":3444,"_807":3445,"_920":1050,"_2871":3499,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":3497,"_901":3500,"_892":3501,"_881":3502,"_816":3503,"_867":3504,"_857":3505},[3449,3450,3451,3452,3453,3454,3455,3456,3457,3458,3459,3460,3461,3462,3463,3464,3465,3466,3467,3468],{"_837":805,"_843":3444,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3445,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":3498,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3497,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3492,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3488,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3484,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3480,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3475,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3471,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3470},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":235,"_191":3469,"_193":234,"_816":236,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":200},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/moonlight-mayhem-codex.webp",[1650],[3472,3473,3474],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},{"_841":861,"_809":862},{"_841":1849,"_809":1850},[3476],{"_841":3477,"_809":3478,"_870":3479},"Read the published Codex transcript","https://github.com/simonw/raccoon-heist-codex/blob/main/transcript.md","The creator links this development record from the build account; it accompanies the game source rather than a generator-only repository.",[3481],{"_841":1457,"_809":3482,"_870":3483},"https://github.com/simonw/raccoon-heist-codex/","Actual game source, committed textures, vendored Three.js, build notes, and transcript. No build step is required; use a local static HTTP server to run the repository.",[3485],{"_841":3486,"_809":236,"_870":3487},"Play Moonlight & Mayhem","Desktop: WASD or arrows to move, E to interact, Space or Shift to dash, Escape to pause. Mobile uses a touch stick and action buttons. Requires a WebGL-capable browser.",[3489],{"_841":3490,"_809":3491,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s build and fix log","https://simonwillison.net/2026/Aug/7/moonlight-mayhem/",[3493,3494,3495,3496],"Play the heist and trace crew rescue, security detection, interactions, and escape.","Read the creator’s build account and compare the original brief with the result.","Follow the transcript and commit history to study scene construction, generated art, and the visual bug fix.","Serve the complete repository locally, then study one mechanic and its supporting assets.","Simon Willison documents giving Codex the game brief and image-generation access, then requesting a visual bug fix. The published project includes the game, generated textures, and the development transcript.",[3238],[3238],[3493,3494,3495,3496],{"_841":3490,"_809":3491,"_802":1230},{"_841":3486,"_809":236,"_802":974,"_870":3487},{"_841":1457,"_809":3482,"_932":933,"_870":3483},{"_841":3477,"_809":3478,"_870":3479},[696,931,1879],"example:dinosaur-offline-gemini-cli","Dinosaur Game Offline: Gemini CLI-assisted runner","Jump a pixel dinosaur over cacti and avoid flying obstacles while the score and speed increase. This small browser game includes its complete JavaScript implementation, sprites, and sound effects.","/examples/dinosaur-offline-gemini-cli/",{"_804":95,"_805":3507,"_807":3508,"_920":3561,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":3560,"_901":3562,"_892":3563,"_881":3564,"_816":3565,"_867":3566,"_857":3567},[3512,3513,3514,3515,3516,3517,3518,3519,3520,3521,3522,3523,3524,3525,3526,3527,3528,3529,3530],{"_837":805,"_843":3507,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3508,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3561,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3560,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3554,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3551,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3547,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3542,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3537,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3534,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3532},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":417,"_191":3531,"_193":416,"_816":418,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":419},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/dinosaur-offline-gemini-cli.webp",[3533],"Gemini CLI",[3535],{"_841":3533,"_809":3536},"/resources/gemini-cli/",[3538],{"_841":3539,"_809":3540,"_870":3541},"See the creator’s Gemini CLI disclosure","https://github.com/tonidevvn/dinosaur-game-offline#how-gemini-cli-helped","README, repository description, and the in-game footer explicitly name gemini-cli. This establishes creator attribution rather than independent proof of fully autonomous generation.",[3543],{"_841":3544,"_809":3545,"_870":3546},"Open the complete dinosaur game source","https://github.com/tonidevvn/dinosaur-game-offline","Complete index.html, style.css, script.js, and referenced image/audio assets. Public source is available, but the repository does not declare a code license.",[3548],{"_841":3549,"_809":418,"_870":3550},"Play Dinosaur Game Offline","Author-hosted browser build; earlier catalog notes report a Chromium check, not independently revalidated here. Space starts and jumps; after a collision, click the restart icon. Desktop keyboard recommended because the board has a fixed 900-pixel width. The full project can also run locally by opening index.html.",[3552],{"_841":3553,"_809":3540,"_870":-7},"Read how Gemini CLI helped",[3555,3556,3557,3558,3559],"Open the author-hosted browser game on a desktop with a keyboard. Press Space once to start, then press Space again to jump over an approaching cactus.","Watch the score rise, test a collision, and use the restart icon after game over. Earlier catalog notes report a start/jump/score/collision/restart smoke test and a preview captured during a jump. That run was not repeated or independently validated in this source-only review.","To run locally, download the complete dinosaur-game-offline repository and open index.html. Keep style.css, script.js, and public/ beside it. No npm installation, build step, Gemini CLI, or API key is needed to play.","If a browser restricts local files, serve the repository with python3 -m http.server 8080 and open http://localhost:8080. The game board is fixed at 900 pixels wide and targets desktop keyboard play. Its optional Google Fonts stylesheet uses the network.","Read the creator’s disclosure, then inspect script.js for the requestAnimationFrame loop, jump state, obstacle spawning, scoring, collision checks, and restart behavior.","The creator explicitly credits Gemini CLI with scaffolding, game logic, debugging, and improvements in the README and game footer. No original conversation or exact model identifier is published; this is a documented assisted build.","DOM / CSS · JavaScript",[3555,3556,3557,3558,3559],{"_841":3553,"_809":3540,"_802":891},{"_841":3549,"_809":418,"_802":974,"_870":3550},{"_841":3544,"_809":3545,"_870":3546,"_932":933},{"_841":3539,"_809":3540,"_870":3541},[706],"example:cloud-crush-gemini-cli","Cloud Crush: Gemini CLI builds a match-3 game","Match cloud-service icons on an eight-by-eight board, chase a timed high score, and create special Gemini gems. Google publishes the complete Go game alongside a detailed Gemini CLI codelab.","/examples/cloud-crush-gemini-cli/",{"_804":93,"_805":3569,"_807":3570,"_920":3627,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":3626,"_901":3628,"_892":3629,"_881":3630,"_816":3631,"_867":3632,"_857":3633},[3574,3575,3576,3577,3578,3579,3580,3581,3582,3583,3584,3585,3586,3587,3588,3589,3590,3591,3592,3593],{"_837":805,"_843":3569,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3570,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3627,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3626,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3619,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3615,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":892,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1532,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3610,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3605,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3600,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3598,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3597},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":422,"_191":3596,"_193":421,"_816":423,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":200},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":3594},[3595],{"_841":1368,"_809":424},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/cloud-crush-gemini-cli.webp",[3533],[3599],{"_841":3533,"_809":3536},[3601],{"_841":3602,"_809":3603,"_870":3604},"See Google’s explicit Gemini CLI attribution","https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/devrel-demos/blob/main/codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang/README.md","The publisher README explicitly names Gemini CLI; the separate official codelab records the development prompts and human steering workflow.",[3606],{"_841":3607,"_809":3608,"_870":3609},"Open the complete Go game project","https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/devrel-demos/tree/main/codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang","Includes main.go, source images and audio, go.mod, browser entry and runtime helper, server/main.go, Dockerfile, and publisher screenshots. The repository code is Apache-2.0. A WASM binary must be built locally.",[3611],{"_841":3612,"_809":3613,"_870":3614},"Download & run Cloud Crush","https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/devrel-demos/blob/main/codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang/README.md#local-development","Local Go / WASM project; no hosted public game endpoint was verified. Use Go 1.26.2+ and run go run . from the game directory. Expand the steps for the complete browser build, asset copy, matching wasm_exec.js, and local server commands. Native play needs a graphical desktop and working audio drivers. Cloud Crush was not compiled locally in this review.",[3616],{"_841":3617,"_809":3618,"_870":-7},"Follow Google’s Gemini CLI game codelab","https://codelabs.developers.google.com/next26/gemini-cli-match3-golang",[3620,3621,3622,3623,3624,3625],"Download the devrel-demos repository and enter codelabs/gemini-cli/gemini-cli-match3-golang. Install Go 1.26.2 or newer; the README’s 1.24+ prerequisite is outdated. For native desktop play, run: go run .","Follow the title and player-name prompts. Use arrow keys to move the cursor and Space to select a gem, then an arrow to swap. Mouse/touch input is also implemented. Compare matching, falling tiles, time bonuses, and score behavior with main.go.","For a local browser build, first prepare the files served by the Go server: mkdir -p public/assets; cp assets/* public/assets/; cp index.html public/index.html. The committed public/assets directory is missing source files required by the game, including background.jpg.","Use the WASM helper from the same Go installation as the compiler: cp \"$(go env GOROOT)/lib/wasm/wasm_exec.js\" public/wasm_exec.js. Then compile: GOOS=js GOARCH=wasm go build -o public/cloud-crush.wasm .","Run the browser server from the same game directory: go run server/main.go. Open http://localhost:8080. Local play does not require Gemini CLI, an API key, a Google Cloud account, or cloud deployment.","Read the official codelab to trace the development prompts. The browser instructions above were checked against source; this review did not install Go or compile the game. Its preview is a publisher-provided gameplay screenshot.","Google’s repository attributes game generation to Gemini CLI. The official codelab shows human orchestration through plan mode, steering prompts, browser adaptation, testing, and subagents. That is publisher evidence, not an independent measurement of autonomous authorship.","Ebitengine 2 · Go / WebAssembly",[3620,3621,3622,3623,3624,3625],{"_841":3617,"_809":3618,"_802":892},{"_841":3612,"_809":3613,"_802":880,"_870":3614},{"_841":3607,"_809":3608,"_870":3609,"_932":933},{"_841":3602,"_809":3603,"_870":3604},[706],"example:roo-code-action","Action with AI: a Roo Code experiment","A small SVG top-down action prototype with mouse-aimed shooting, enemies and telegraphed attacks, paired with a detailed account of prompt-driven implementation.","/examples/roo-code-action/",{"_804":91,"_805":3635,"_807":3636,"_920":3684,"_916":922,"_908":3683,"_901":3685,"_892":3686,"_881":3687,"_816":3688,"_867":3689,"_912":923,"_857":3690},[3640,3641,3642,3643,3644,3645,3646,3647,3648,3649,3650,3651,3652,3653,3654,3655,3656,3657],{"_837":805,"_843":3635,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3636,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3684,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3683,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3678,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3675,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3671,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3666,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3661,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3659},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":427,"_191":3658,"_193":426,"_816":428,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/roo-code-action.webp",[3660],"Roo Code",[3662],{"_841":3663,"_809":3664,"_870":3665},"Read the original AI development account","https://zenn.dev/mizchi/articles/game-with-cline","The author names Roo Code and Claude 3.5 Sonnet, explains the no-direct-coding constraint and documents the human design and steering role.",[3667],{"_841":3668,"_809":3669,"_870":3670},"Open the complete action prototype","https://github.com/mizchi/action-with-ai","Complete React/TypeScript project with SVG rendering, movement, collision, combat, shared types, tests and development notes. No repository license file was found in the reviewed tree.",[3672],{"_841":3673,"_809":428,"_870":3674},"Play Action with AI","Early desktop keyboard-and-mouse prototype. WASD moves and holding the mouse button fires; visual polish and a full commercial campaign are outside its scope.",[3676],{"_841":3677,"_809":3664,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s Roo Code experiment",[3679,3680,3681,3682],"Move with WASD, aim with the mouse and hold the mouse button to shoot.","Read the original sequence from rendering and movement through enemy health and attack warnings.","Inspect docs/overview.md, the shared types and combat modules alongside the creator’s discussion of documentation drift.","For local study, install the project dependencies with the documented pnpm setup and run pnpm dev, then change one attack or movement rule.","Mizchi explicitly used Roo Code, formerly Roo Cline, with Claude 3.5 Sonnet while forbidding direct human code edits. The human supplied an experienced developer’s design, incremental instructions and architecture constraints. The published article includes the workflow and limitations; this is an early prototype.","React · SVG · TypeScript",[3679,3680,3681,3682],{"_841":3677,"_809":3664,"_802":1230},{"_841":3673,"_809":428,"_802":974,"_870":3674},{"_841":3668,"_809":3669,"_870":3670,"_932":933},{"_841":3663,"_809":3664,"_870":3665},[],"example:three-quake-claude-port","Three Quake: an AI-assisted Quake port","Play Quake’s shareware episode in a Three.js browser port, and study how an existing shooter’s rendering and runtime were adapted with AI assistance.","/examples/three-quake-claude-port/",{"_804":89,"_805":3692,"_807":3693,"_920":1050,"_916":1051,"_908":3743,"_901":3744,"_892":3745,"_881":3746,"_816":3747,"_867":3748,"_857":3749,"_912":923},[3697,3698,3699,3700,3701,3702,3703,3704,3705,3706,3707,3708,3709,3710,3711,3712,3713,3714,3715],{"_837":805,"_843":3692,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3693,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3743,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3738,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3734,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3730,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3725,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3720,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3718,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3717},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":431,"_191":3716,"_193":430,"_816":432,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/three-quake-claude-port.webp",[1023],[3719],{"_841":861,"_809":862},[3721],{"_841":3722,"_809":3723,"_870":3724},"Read the author’s AI and original-game credits","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#credits","The maintainer distinguishes id Software’s original game from the Three.js port made with Claude assistance.",[3726],{"_841":3727,"_809":3728,"_870":3729},"Open the complete browser port","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake","Complete browser port, maps, runtime source and tests, with the shareware pak0.pak. Code is GPL-2.0; original Quake game data has separate terms and is not relicensed by the code license.",[3731],{"_841":3732,"_809":432,"_870":3733},"Play Three Quake","Keyboard, mouse and a WebGL-capable browser. The included shareware data covers Episode 1; full-game content is separate.",[3735],{"_841":3736,"_809":3737,"_870":-7},"Read the port credits and creator dev log","https://github.com/mrdoob/three-quake#dev-log",[3739,3740,3741,3742],"Open the browser build, start a new single-player game and test the movement and firing controls.","Read the creator’s port credits and dev log alongside the original id Software source reference.","Inspect the browser renderer, game runtime, maps and tests to trace how the existing game was adapted.","Use the included shareware data for Episode 1; a registered full-game data set is separate and must be supplied by its owner.","Mr.doob credits Claude for assistance with the Three.js port. Quake’s game design and original implementation belong to id Software; this is an AI-assisted port, not a claim that AI created Quake. The README links a creator dev log without identifying a particular Claude client.",[3739,3740,3741,3742],{"_841":3736,"_809":3737,"_802":891},{"_841":3732,"_809":432,"_802":974,"_870":3733},{"_841":3727,"_809":3728,"_870":3729,"_932":933},{"_841":3722,"_809":3723,"_870":3724},[931],"example:crown-defender-codex","Crown Defender TD 3D · Codex build","Control a hero under an isometric camera, defend a castle through thirty waves and choose upgrades to unlock a cosmetic crown.","/examples/crown-defender-codex/",{"_804":87,"_805":3751,"_807":3752,"_920":1050,"_916":1051,"_912":1743,"_908":3802,"_901":3803,"_892":3804,"_881":3805,"_816":3806,"_867":3807,"_857":3808},[3756,3757,3758,3759,3760,3761,3762,3763,3764,3765,3766,3767,3768,3769,3770,3771,3772,3773,3774],{"_837":805,"_843":3751,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3752,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":1742,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3802,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3797,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3794,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":889,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3789,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3785,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3780,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3777,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3776},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":435,"_191":3775,"_193":434,"_816":436,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":848},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":437},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/crown-defender-codex.webp",[1650],[3778,3779],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},{"_841":861,"_809":862},[3781],{"_841":3782,"_809":3783,"_870":3784},"Read the author’s agent attribution","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/blob/main/COMPARISON.md","Author-published Russian comparison explicitly states that Codex built this version from the same requirements as the Claude Code project; no raw session is published.",[3786],{"_841":3787,"_809":436,"_870":3788},"Open the complete Codex game project","Includes game.js, interface, bundled Three.js, runtime textures, requirements and optional WebSocket relay. No build or dependency installation for solo play. MIT code; see ASSET_CREDITS.md.",[3790],{"_841":3791,"_809":3792,"_870":3793},"Download and run Crown Defender","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","Static browser game. Run python3 -m http.server 8010 and open localhost:8010/index.html; choose Играть (Play). Russian interface. WASD/arrows move; semicolon attacks. Mobile joystick/buttons included. Optional two-player mode requires node server/multiplayer-server.mjs.",[3795],{"_841":3796,"_809":3783,"_870":-7},"Read the same-brief agent comparison",[3798,3799,3800,3801],"Serve the project locally and enter TD Defense.","Read the original requirements and same-brief comparison.","Inspect hero movement, wave progression and upgrade logic.","Change one upgrade and test losing, retrying and saved progress.","Aleksandr-Litvinenko attributes this build to Codex and publishes a comparison with a Claude Code version made from the same brief. The author states that the comparison concerns the agents’ original implementation choices, with assets and runtime code included here.",[3798,3799,3800,3801],{"_841":3796,"_809":3783,"_802":1230},{"_841":3791,"_809":3792,"_802":880,"_870":3793},{"_841":3787,"_809":436,"_932":933,"_870":3788},{"_841":3782,"_809":3783,"_870":3784},[696,931],"example:arkanoid-neon-claude","Arkanoid Neon","Bounce the ball through eight neon brick layouts, collect power-ups and keep the rally alive as the stages accelerate. This complete browser game uses Canvas 2D and synthesized Web Audio.","/examples/arkanoid-neon-claude/",{"_804":85,"_805":3810,"_807":3811,"_920":3864,"_916":922,"_912":1743,"_908":3863,"_901":3865,"_892":3866,"_881":3867,"_816":3868,"_867":3869,"_857":3870},[3815,3816,3817,3818,3819,3820,3821,3822,3823,3824,3825,3826,3827,3828,3829,3830,3831,3832,3833,3834],{"_837":805,"_843":3810,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3811,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3864,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":1742,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3863,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3858,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3855,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":2219,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3850,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3845,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3841,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3839,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3838},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":440,"_191":3837,"_193":439,"_816":441,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":3835},[3836],{"_841":1368,"_809":442},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/arkanoid-neon-claude.webp",[1190],[3840],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},[3842],{"_841":3843,"_809":441,"_870":3844},"Read the creator’s Claude Code attribution","The creator directly names Claude Code and its model, separates the original request from the finished project, and describes code-generated art/audio. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[3846],{"_841":3847,"_809":3848,"_870":3849},"Open the complete browser game","https://github.com/Jack-c3l2w/arkanoid-neon","Complete index.html, style.css and game.js with procedural graphics and audio; open index.html locally, no build step. Google Fonts is optional and falls back to system fonts offline. No root LICENSE was found. Fan project inspired by Arkanoid, not affiliated with Taito.",[3851],{"_841":3852,"_809":3853,"_870":3854},"Play Arkanoid Neon","https://jack-c3l2w.github.io/arkanoid-neon/","Mouse, arrows or A/D move; click/Space launches and fires; P/Esc pauses. Touch drag and tap are supported.",[3856],{"_841":3857,"_809":441,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s original request",[3859,3860,3861,3862],"Play a stage and compare paddle control, collision behavior, power-ups and losing a life.","Read the creator’s original Swedish request and AI attribution.","Open index.html locally and trace the game loop, level data and procedural graphics in game.js.","Ask an agent to change one brick pattern or power-up, then test launching, losing a life and restarting.","The creator’s Swedish README attributes the code, graphics, sound, music and levels to Claude Code using Claude Opus 5.5, and publishes the original one-sentence request. Treat this as a creator build disclosure, not an independently audited generation transcript.","Custom Canvas 2D · JavaScript · Web Audio",[3859,3860,3861,3862],{"_841":3857,"_809":441,"_802":2219},{"_841":3852,"_809":3853,"_802":974,"_870":3854},{"_841":3847,"_809":3848,"_932":933,"_870":3849},{"_841":3843,"_809":441,"_870":3844},[694],"example:supermarket-simulator-cursor","Supermarket Simulator","Manage a supermarket in first person: order goods, unpack deliveries, stock shelves and serve customers. The creator built this Unity experiment with Cursor and generated the 3D models with Hunyuan.","/examples/supermarket-simulator-cursor/",{"_804":83,"_805":3872,"_807":3873,"_920":3927,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":3926,"_901":3928,"_892":3929,"_881":3930,"_816":3931,"_867":3932,"_857":3933},[3877,3878,3879,3880,3881,3882,3883,3884,3885,3886,3887,3888,3889,3890,3891,3892,3893,3894,3895,3896],{"_837":805,"_843":3872,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3873,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3927,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3926,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3921,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3918,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1397,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3913,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3909,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3905,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3901,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3900},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":445,"_191":3899,"_193":444,"_816":446,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":3897},[3898],{"_841":1368,"_809":447},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/supermarket-simulator-cursor.webp",[1257],[3902],{"_841":3903,"_809":3904},"Unity · Manual","/resources/unity-engine/",[3906],{"_841":3907,"_809":446,"_870":3908},"Read the creator’s AI attribution","Author README names coding models, Hunyuan assets, source setup and a linked creation video. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[3910],{"_841":1457,"_809":3911,"_870":3912},"https://github.com/breineng/supermarket-simulator","Complete Unity 2023.2.6f1 project with Assets, Packages and ProjectSettings. Scenes, prefabs and models use Git LFS: clone with LFS and run git lfs pull before opening Assets/Scenes/InitScene.unity. MIT code; Unity, generated models and dependencies retain their terms. LFS objects were not fetched in this review.",[3914],{"_841":3915,"_809":3916,"_870":3917},"Download the Windows game","https://github.com/breineng/supermarket-simulator/releases/download/0.0.1/SupermarketSimulator.zip","Windows download, about 397 MB, from release 0.0.1. Extract and run Supermaket Simulator.exe. Other platforms require a source build; the binary was not downloaded or executed in this review.",[3919],{"_841":3920,"_809":446,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s development disclosure",[3922,3923,3924,3925],"Download the Windows release and try the order, delivery, stocking and checkout loop.","Read the creator’s build account and linked video to separate coding assistance from generated models.","Clone with Git LFS, fetch the LFS objects and open InitScene in the matching Unity editor.","Adjust one stock, customer or checkout behavior with an agent, then compare a complete customer-service loop.","The author names Cursor with Gemini 2.5 Pro, Claude Opus 4 and Claude Sonnet 4, and links a creation video. The fully AI-generated description is a creator claim; the public source separates the Unity project and Hunyuan model work.","Unity 2023.2.6f1 · URP · C#",[3922,3923,3924,3925],{"_841":3920,"_809":446,"_802":891},{"_841":3915,"_809":3916,"_802":880,"_870":3917},{"_841":1457,"_809":3911,"_870":3912,"_932":933},{"_841":3907,"_809":446,"_870":3908},[3934],"unity-engine","example:magic-carpet-wizard-astra","Magic Carpet Wizard · A Thousand Skies","Fly a carpet over a tiny spherical world, thread scoring rings, cast three spells and face roaming enemies and bosses. Local ghost races let two players take turns.","/examples/magic-carpet-wizard-astra/",{"_804":81,"_805":3936,"_807":3937,"_920":1050,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":3985,"_901":3986,"_892":3987,"_881":3988,"_816":3989,"_867":3990,"_857":3991},[3941,3942,3943,3944,3945,3946,3947,3948,3949,3950,3951,3952,3953,3954,3955,3956,3957,3958,3959],{"_837":805,"_843":3936,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3937,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":3985,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":3980,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":3977,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":3973,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":3969,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":3964,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":3962,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":3961},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":450,"_191":3960,"_193":449,"_816":451,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":452},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/magic-carpet-wizard-astra.webp",[1779],[3963],{"_841":861,"_809":862},[3965],{"_841":3966,"_809":3967,"_870":3968},"See the creator’s Astra attribution","https://github.com/threapchills/MagicCarpetWizard","The author-controlled repository description names GPT-6 Astra. It does not establish which coding-agent client was used or publish the initial session.",[3970],{"_841":3971,"_809":3967,"_870":3972},"Open the complete carpet-flight project","Flight, enemies, spells, procedural world, audio, races and tests. Node.js 22; npm ci then npm run dev. No API keys; optional Google Fonts fall back to system fonts.",[3974],{"_841":3975,"_809":451,"_870":3976},"Play Magic Carpet Wizard","Desktop WebGL2, mouse and keyboard. Enter starts; WASD steers/climbs, mouse plus left click aims/casts, 1–3 changes spells, Space rolls, Shift boosts, and R retries.",[3978],{"_841":3979,"_809":3967,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s implementation guide",[3981,3982,3983,3984],"Play an adventure run and test flight and spells.","Read the creator’s attribution and audio notes.","Inspect flight rules, collision and rendering modules.","Adjust one obstacle or spell and test a retry and ghost race.","The creator’s repository About section attributes the game to GPT-6 Astra. The README documents original procedural geometry and textures plus supplied audio; it does not publish prompts, a transcript or an exact division of human and model work.",[3981,3982,3983,3984],{"_841":3979,"_809":3967,"_802":891},{"_841":3975,"_809":451,"_802":974,"_870":3976},{"_841":3971,"_809":3967,"_932":933,"_870":3972},{"_841":3966,"_809":3967,"_870":3968},[931],"example:sakura-crossing-qwen","3D Sakura Crossing: an exploration prototype","Explore a cel-shaded Japanese neighbourhood with a working railway crossing, residents, a lifting bridge, a drivable car, and a swimmable river.","/examples/sakura-crossing-qwen/",{"_804":79,"_805":3993,"_807":3994,"_920":1050,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":4046,"_901":4047,"_892":4048,"_881":4049,"_816":4050,"_867":4051,"_857":4052},[3998,3999,4000,4001,4002,4003,4004,4005,4006,4007,4008,4009,4010,4011,4012,4013,4014,4015,4016,4017],{"_837":805,"_843":3993,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":3994,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4046,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4041,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4037,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4032,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4029,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4024,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4022,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4021},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":455,"_191":4020,"_193":454,"_816":456,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4018},[4019],{"_841":1368,"_809":457},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/sakura-crossing-qwen.webp",[1190],[4023],{"_841":861,"_809":862},[4025],{"_841":4026,"_809":4027,"_870":4028},"Read the Qwen and human contribution credit","https://github.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing#credits","README explicitly distinguishes locally generated Qwen code from human review, debugging, and extensions. The creator’s linked Reddit build account identifies Claude Code CLI as the harness, not the Claude model.",[4030],{"_841":2275,"_809":456,"_870":4031},"GPL-3.0 source with complete index.html, vendored Three.js, procedural textures, and implementation notes. Run python3 -m http.server 5191 and open localhost:5191/index.html; file:// loading is unsupported. The original author has ended active development. The creator describes an exploration prototype, not a finished campaign; no complete win/loss loop is claimed.",[4033],{"_841":4034,"_809":4035,"_870":4036},"Explore Sakura Crossing","https://danymaniglie-cmyk.github.io/3d-sakura-crossing/","Exploration prototype. WASD walks, Shift runs, mouse drag looks, E talks, F enters/exits the car, and Space/C swims up/down. Touch controls included; mobile performance remains limited.",[4038],{"_841":4039,"_809":4040,"_870":-7},"Read the rendering and implementation recipe","https://github.com/danymaniglie-cmyk/3d-sakura-crossing/blob/main/CARTOON.md",[4042,4043,4044,4045],"Explore the browser world on foot, then try the car, river, and moving bridge.","Read the credits and the author’s account of using a local Qwen model through Claude Code CLI.","Inspect CARTOON.md and the complete index.html plus vendored Three.js dependency.","Serve a local copy over HTTP, change one interaction, and verify movement and collisions.","The repository credits code generation to locally running Qwen 3.8 27B, followed by human review, debugging, and extensions. In the linked build account the author identifies Claude Code CLI as the harness with Qwen as its model.",[4042,4043,4044,4045],{"_841":4039,"_809":4040,"_802":1230},{"_841":4034,"_809":4035,"_802":974,"_870":4036},{"_841":2275,"_809":456,"_932":933,"_870":4031},{"_841":4026,"_809":4027,"_870":4028},[931],"example:claude-dreaming-godot","Claude Dreaming","Walk from a pixel-art attic into playable 3D paintings: a dream garden, space flight, small planets, and community-built rooms.","/examples/claude-dreaming-godot/",{"_804":77,"_805":4054,"_807":4055,"_920":3433,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":4106,"_901":4107,"_892":4108,"_881":4109,"_816":4110,"_867":4111,"_857":4112},[4059,4060,4061,4062,4063,4064,4065,4066,4067,4068,4069,4070,4071,4072,4073,4074,4075,4076,4077,4078],{"_837":805,"_843":4054,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4055,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":3433,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4106,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4101,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4097,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":892,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4093,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4089,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4085,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4083,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4082},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":460,"_191":4081,"_193":459,"_816":461,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4079},[4080],{"_841":1368,"_809":462},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/claude-dreaming-godot.webp",[1023],[4084],{"_841":1448,"_809":1449},[4086],{"_841":4087,"_809":461,"_870":4088},"Read the creator’s AI contribution disclosure","The creator explicitly credits Claude and discloses assisted code, graphics, sounds, and text. This is an author disclosure and contribution workflow, not a complete development transcript.",[4090],{"_841":1589,"_809":4091,"_870":4092},"https://github.com/moritzfh/claude-dreaming","Full scenes, GDScript, levels, rooms, assets, film intro, and export presets. Run with Godot 4.7.2 standard: import project.godot and press F5. Code is MIT; original assets are CC BY 4.0, while film material and film-derived art have project-only restrictions in NOTICE.md.",[4094],{"_841":4095,"_809":461,"_870":4096},"Play Claude Dreaming","In-development HTML5 game. WASD moves; mouse looks, Space jumps/glides, E enters paintings, R respawns, and Esc pauses. Menus are German; Claude speaks English. The film intro can be skipped.",[4098],{"_841":4099,"_809":4100,"_870":-7},"Read how to add a dream with Claude","https://github.com/moritzfh/claude-dreaming/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md",[4102,4103,4104,4105],"Start the browser build; hold Enter to skip the film if desired.","Enter a painting and compare its movement with the attic and community rooms.","Import the full project in Godot 4.7.2 standard, then read the level template and contribution guide.","Create one small level through the published API and test entry, movement, respawn, and returning to the attic.","Rusty credits the game to Rusty and Claude and discloses AI assistance for code, graphics, sounds, and text. The repository provides contribution instructions and a level API for building further dreams with Claude.",[4102,4103,4104,4105],{"_841":4099,"_809":4100,"_802":892},{"_841":4095,"_809":461,"_802":974,"_870":4096},{"_841":1589,"_809":4091,"_932":933,"_870":4092},{"_841":4087,"_809":461,"_870":4088},[1481],"example:sprout-quest-claude","Sprout Quest","Explore a small world, fight real-time arena battles, gather materials, craft gear and rebuild a village. Sprout Quest is a mobile-first adventure with a 2D world and live-rendered 3D characters and items.","/examples/sprout-quest-claude/",{"_804":75,"_805":4114,"_807":4115,"_920":4170,"_2871":4171,"_916":922,"_912":1743,"_908":4168,"_901":4172,"_892":4173,"_881":4174,"_816":4175,"_867":4176,"_857":4177},[4119,4120,4121,4122,4123,4124,4125,4126,4127,4128,4129,4130,4131,4132,4133,4134,4135,4136,4137,4138,4139],{"_837":805,"_843":4114,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4115,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4170,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":4169,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":1742,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4168,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4163,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4161,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4156,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4152,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4148,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4144,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4143},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":465,"_191":4142,"_193":464,"_816":466,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4140},[4141],{"_841":1368,"_809":467},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/sprout-quest-claude.webp",[1190],[4145,4146,4147],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":861,"_809":862},{"_841":2843,"_809":2844},[4149],{"_841":3907,"_809":4150,"_870":4151},"https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest#how-it-was-built","README separates the original build from later human playtest/AI iteration; publishes source modules, generated models and runtime assets, plus a prompt summary. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[4153],{"_841":1457,"_809":4154,"_870":4155},"https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest","Complete game code, runtime GLBs/sprite atlases, Blender scripts and tests. bun install then bun run dev opens localhost:3000; normal builds use committed art and do not require Blender. No root LICENSE was found, so public source visibility does not establish broad reuse permission.",[4157],{"_841":4158,"_809":4159,"_870":4160},"Play Sprout Quest","https://aibengineering.github.io/sprout-quest/","Author-hosted browser adventure designed for portrait phones, with desktop keyboard controls and localStorage saves.",[4162],{"_841":2158,"_809":4150,"_870":-7},[4164,4165,4166,4167],"Play the portrait-browser prologue and follow its first fight, gathering and forge tasks.","Read the build account to see how human phone playtests guided later Claude Code changes.","Run bun install and bun run dev; inspect the game modules, committed runtime assets and Blender builders.","Change one combat, crafting or story rule with an agent, then replay the affected progression and save flow.","The creator says Claude Code generated the game, tests and Blender art pipeline from plain-language requests while the human played on a phone and gave feedback. The repository contains the runtime art as well as its source builders.",[2843],"Custom Canvas 2D + Three.js · TypeScript",[2843],[4164,4165,4166,4167],{"_841":2158,"_809":4150,"_802":1230},{"_841":4158,"_809":4159,"_802":974,"_870":4160},{"_841":1457,"_809":4154,"_870":4155,"_932":933},{"_841":3907,"_809":4150,"_870":4151},[694,931,2881],"example:mosswing-astra","Mosswing","Keep a small creature airborne with one-tap flaps, pass scrolling stone gaps and chase a higher score in a compact 3D browser game.","/examples/mosswing-astra/",{"_804":73,"_805":4179,"_807":4180,"_920":4227,"_916":1051,"_912":1743,"_908":4226,"_901":4228,"_892":4229,"_881":4230,"_816":4231,"_867":4232,"_857":4233},[4184,4185,4186,4187,4188,4189,4190,4191,4192,4193,4194,4195,4196,4197,4198,4199,4200,4201],{"_837":805,"_843":4179,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4180,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4227,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":1742,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4226,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4221,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4218,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":2219,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4214,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4209,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4204,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4203},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":470,"_191":4202,"_193":469,"_816":471,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":472},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/mosswing-astra.webp",[1779],[4205],{"_841":4206,"_809":4207,"_870":4208},"Read the creator’s test and prompt","https://github.com/Ayi1337/gpt6-astra-one-shot-games#02--mosswing","The author labels this an Astra one-shot test and preserves the initial instructions and generated artifact. The coding-agent client is not identified.",[4210],{"_841":4211,"_809":4212,"_870":4213},"Open the complete Mosswing source","https://github.com/Ayi1337/gpt6-astra-one-shot-games/tree/main/mosswing","Contains the complete standalone HTML and separate source files. No package installation or build step is required. A public source license was not observed.",[4215],{"_841":4216,"_809":471,"_870":4217},"Play Mosswing","Designed for a mobile browser with one-tap control. The repository also supplies a standalone mosswing.html that can be opened in a modern browser without installation.",[4219],{"_841":4220,"_809":4207,"_870":-7},"Read the original one-shot prompt",[4222,4223,4224,4225],"Play and identify gravity, flap impulse and scoring.","Read the original prompt alongside the single HTML result.","Inspect the separate source folder before editing.","Change one flight parameter and compare collision and restart behavior.","Ayi1337 publishes the original Astra prompt and resulting standalone HTML, reporting a one-shot Xhigh test. The human specified tap-to-flap rules and requested an original character, world and visual style; this is a creator claim, not an audited generation trace.","Three.js · JavaScript · WebGL",[4222,4223,4224,4225],{"_841":4220,"_809":4207,"_802":2219},{"_841":4216,"_809":471,"_802":974,"_870":4217},{"_841":4211,"_809":4212,"_932":933,"_870":4213},{"_841":4206,"_809":4207,"_870":4208},[],"example:astra-floor-ai","Astra Floor","Fight six zombie waves and a final boss in a first-person industrial arena, managing ammunition, recoil, stamina and purchases between rounds.","/examples/astra-floor-ai/",{"_804":71,"_805":4235,"_807":4236,"_920":4289,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":4288,"_901":4290,"_892":4291,"_881":4292,"_816":4293,"_867":4294,"_857":4295},[4240,4241,4242,4243,4244,4245,4246,4247,4248,4249,4250,4251,4252,4253,4254,4255,4256,4257,4258,4259],{"_837":805,"_843":4235,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4236,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4289,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4288,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4283,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4280,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4275,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4270,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4266,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4264,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4263},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":475,"_191":4262,"_193":474,"_816":476,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4260},[4261],{"_841":1368,"_809":477},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/astra-floor-ai.webp",[1578,2714],[4265],{"_841":861,"_809":862},[4267],{"_841":4268,"_809":476,"_870":4269},"Read the author’s division of AI work","The repository owner’s submission distinguishes Astra from Antigravity work. The README also credits both tools; no full conversation archive is supplied.",[4271],{"_841":4272,"_809":4273,"_870":4274},"Open the complete FPS project","https://github.com/BEROCHLU/astrafloor","Game implementation, procedural models, bundled textures/music and tests. Node.js 22.13+; npm install then npm run dev. Third-party texture credits are documented separately.",[4276],{"_841":4277,"_809":4278,"_870":4279},"Play Astra Floor","https://astrafloor.berochlu.workers.dev/","Desktop WebGL, keyboard and mouse. Wait for INITIALIZING to finish, choose a difficulty, then DEPLOY. WASD moves, mouse aims/fires, R reloads, Q heals, G throws a grenade, and V uses melee. Runs are not saved. The in-app browser could not capture the mouse during review; a normal desktop browser is recommended.",[4281],{"_841":4282,"_809":476,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s AI development disclosure",[4284,4285,4286,4287],"Choose Normal difficulty and enter the first wave.","Read the creator’s architecture and model disclosure.","Inspect procedural weapons, enemies and audio implementation.","Tune one weapon or enemy and verify a wave and shop transition.","BEROCHLU credits GPT-6 Astra with much of the architecture, procedural 3D generation and Web Audio synthesis. Antigravity 2.0 supplied other implementation and iterative refinement. The disclosure does not claim a single-prompt build.","Three.js · TypeScript (React UI)",[4284,4285,4286,4287],{"_841":4282,"_809":476,"_802":891},{"_841":4277,"_809":4278,"_802":974,"_870":4279},{"_841":4272,"_809":4273,"_932":933,"_870":4274},{"_841":4268,"_809":476,"_870":4269},[931],"example:isocoaster-cursor","IsoCoaster","Lay out a theme park with roller coasters, rides and guests. IsoCoaster is a separate playable game and route in the creator’s Cursor-assisted IsoCity repository.","/examples/isocoaster-cursor/",{"_804":69,"_805":4297,"_807":4298,"_920":4345,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4344,"_901":4346,"_892":4347,"_881":4348,"_816":4349,"_867":4350,"_857":4351},[4302,4303,4304,4305,4306,4307,4308,4309,4310,4311,4312,4313,4314,4315,4316,4317,4318,4319,4320],{"_837":805,"_843":4297,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4298,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4345,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4344,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4339,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4337,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4332,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4328,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4325,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4324},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":480,"_191":4323,"_193":479,"_816":481,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4321},[4322],{"_841":1368,"_809":482},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/isocoaster-cursor.webp",[1257],[4326],{"_841":3907,"_809":481,"_870":4327},"README distinguishes the two games, their hosts and separate local routes. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[4329],{"_841":1457,"_809":4330,"_870":4331},"https://github.com/amilich/isometric-city","Complete IsoCity repository includes the dedicated src/app/coaster route, shared components and assets. npm install then npm run dev; open localhost:3000/coaster. MIT code; use a Node runtime compatible with its current Next 16 package.",[4333],{"_841":4334,"_809":4335,"_870":4336},"Play IsoCoaster","https://iso-coaster.com","Author-hosted browser theme-park builder; the shared source repository contains its separate coaster route.",[4338],{"_841":3920,"_809":481,"_870":-7},[4340,4341,4342,4343],"Play the theme park builder and inspect how coaster tracks, rides and guests interact.","Run the repository locally and open /coaster rather than the city-building route.","Compare the coaster-specific state and interface with the shared isometric rendering components.","Ask an agent to adjust one ride or guest behavior, then test construction, simulation and save/load.","The shared creator README attributes both games to Cursor. Study how a common isometric renderer supports a different simulation; the source does not disclose a specific model or a full AI conversation.","Custom Canvas 2D · TypeScript",[4340,4341,4342,4343],{"_841":3920,"_809":481,"_802":891},{"_841":4334,"_809":4335,"_802":974,"_870":4336},{"_841":1457,"_809":4330,"_870":4331,"_932":933},{"_841":3907,"_809":481,"_870":4327},[],"example:spirit-of-kiro","Spirit of Kiro","Find unusual items, combine or transform them on a workshop bench, and sell the results to an AI appraiser in an open-ended crafting game.","/examples/spirit-of-kiro/",{"_804":67,"_805":4353,"_807":4354,"_920":4406,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4405,"_901":4407,"_892":4408,"_881":4409,"_816":4410,"_867":4411,"_857":4412},[4358,4359,4360,4361,4362,4363,4364,4365,4366,4367,4368,4369,4370,4371,4372,4373,4374,4375,4376],{"_837":805,"_843":4353,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4354,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4406,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4405,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4400,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4397,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":892,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":889,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4392,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4387,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4382,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4380},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":485,"_191":4379,"_193":484,"_816":486,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4377},[4378],{"_841":1368,"_809":487},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/spirit-of-kiro.webp",[4381],"Kiro",[4383],{"_841":4384,"_809":4385,"_870":4386},"Read the official Kiro development disclosure","https://github.com/kirodotdev/spirit-of-kiro#spirit-of-kiro","Official creator statement reports more than 95% prompted code. The core crafting loop is complete; roadmap features and intentionally unfinished challenge-branch tasks remain separate.",[4388],{"_841":4389,"_809":4390,"_870":4391},"Open the complete crafting-game project","https://github.com/kirodotdev/spirit-of-kiro","MIT-0 game repository with Vue client, Bun server, item-image service, infrastructure, and deployment documentation. Runtime item text and interactions depend on AWS Bedrock; item-image generation has additional optional model requirements.",[4393],{"_841":4394,"_809":4395,"_870":4396},"Download and run Spirit of Kiro","https://github.com/kirodotdev/spirit-of-kiro/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","No anonymous hosted game is linked by the official project. Local play requires Docker/Podman, an AWS account/credentials and CLI, Bedrock access to supported text models, and deployed Cognito resources. Follow docs/local-setup.md to launch the stack and bootstrap DynamoDB. AWS runtime usage can incur charges; source-checked steps, not executed.",[4398],{"_841":4399,"_809":486,"_870":-7},"Follow the official learn-by-playing guide",[4401,4402,4403,4404],"Read the official setup guide and confirm the AWS model access required for the runtime.","Deploy the Cognito resources, start the client/server stack, and bootstrap the local DynamoDB tables.","Play the discover, craft, and sell loop before attempting the challenge branch.","Follow one guided bug fix or feature change and verify the resulting interaction in the game.","The official Kiro project says more than 95% of its code was written by prompting Kiro. Its guide uses the actual game to teach steering, bug fixes, refactoring, specifications, hooks, and MCP; AI also generates items and crafting outcomes at runtime.","Custom Vue 3 · DOM/CSS sprites · TypeScript",[4401,4402,4403,4404],{"_841":4399,"_809":486,"_802":892},{"_841":4394,"_809":4395,"_802":880,"_870":4396},{"_841":4389,"_809":4390,"_932":933,"_870":4391},{"_841":4384,"_809":4385,"_870":4386},[],"example:rhythm-master-windsurf","Rhythm Master 3D","A four-lane music game with generated synth tracks, difficulty settings, combos and a special mode, implemented as a single browser HTML file.","/examples/rhythm-master-windsurf/",{"_804":65,"_805":4414,"_807":4415,"_920":4466,"_916":1051,"_908":4465,"_901":4467,"_892":4468,"_881":4469,"_816":4470,"_867":4471,"_857":4472,"_912":923},[4419,4420,4421,4422,4423,4424,4425,4426,4427,4428,4429,4430,4431,4432,4433,4434,4435,4436,4437],{"_837":805,"_843":4414,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4415,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4466,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4465,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4460,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4457,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":889,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4452,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4448,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4443,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4441,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4439},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":490,"_191":4438,"_193":489,"_816":491,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":848},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/rhythm-master-windsurf.webp",[4440,1023],"Windsurf",[4442],{"_841":861,"_809":862},[4444],{"_841":4445,"_809":4446,"_870":4447},"Read the author’s AI tools and prompt disclosure","https://www.linkedin.com/posts/frankniu_if-youre-not-vibe-coding-with-claude-sonnet-activity-7304977951761039362-2xQe","The creator identifies Claude Sonnet 3.7, describes passing output into Windsurf, and links the exact rhythm-game repository in the same post.",[4449],{"_841":4450,"_809":491,"_870":4451},"Open the complete rhythm-game source","The full game is rhythm.html, with procedural music and geometry rather than a separate asset download. Third-party libraries load from CDNs. No repository code license is declared.",[4453],{"_841":4454,"_809":4455,"_870":4456},"Download and run Rhythm Master 3D","https://github.com/frankjniu/rhythm-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","No public hosted build was verified. Serve the downloaded directory and open rhythm.html. External CDNs supply Three.js and Tone.js, so internet access is needed; a click starts audio.",[4458],{"_841":4459,"_809":4446,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s build workflow",[4461,4462,4463,4464],"Download the repository and serve its directory with a local HTTP server, then open rhythm.html.","Choose a track and difficulty, start the game, and use D/F/J/K as notes reach the target zone.","Test combo scoring, Escape pause and the Space special mode before changing timing or difficulty.","Compare the single-file implementation with the creator’s original brief and debugging workflow.","Frank Niu links this game from a creator post describing a Claude Sonnet 3.7 web-chat-to-Windsurf workflow: generate an initial game, diagnose issues in chat, then apply changes in Windsurf. It is a human-steered coding example, not evidence that Claude Code or a single autonomous run built it.","Three.js · Tone.js · JavaScript",[4461,4462,4463,4464],{"_841":4459,"_809":4446,"_802":1230},{"_841":4454,"_809":4455,"_802":880,"_870":4456},{"_841":4450,"_809":491,"_870":4451,"_932":933},{"_841":4445,"_809":4446,"_870":4447},[931],"example:pokemon-tactics-claude","Pokemon Tactics","Move Pokemon across an isometric battlefield, use elevation and aim area attacks without hitting allies. This playable tactical fan game combines a TypeScript simulation with 2D-HD sprites on Babylon.js terrain.","/examples/pokemon-tactics-claude/",{"_804":63,"_805":4474,"_807":4475,"_920":4526,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":4525,"_901":4527,"_892":4528,"_881":4529,"_816":4530,"_867":4531,"_857":4532},[4479,4480,4481,4482,4483,4484,4485,4486,4487,4488,4489,4490,4491,4492,4493,4494,4495,4496,4497,4498],{"_837":805,"_843":4474,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4475,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4526,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4525,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4520,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4518,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4513,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4509,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4505,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4503,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4502},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":494,"_191":4501,"_193":493,"_816":495,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4499},[4500],{"_841":1368,"_809":496},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/pokemon-tactics-claude.webp",[1190],[4504],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},[4506],{"_841":3907,"_809":4507,"_870":4508},"https://github.com/kekel87/pokemon-tactics#built-with-ai","Author explains human direction versus generated implementation; independent itch page repeats AI and art disclosure. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[4510],{"_841":1457,"_809":4511,"_870":4512},"https://github.com/kekel87/pokemon-tactics","Complete pnpm workspace with game core, Pokemon data, Babylon renderer, UI and app assets. package.json requires Node >=24 and pnpm 10.32.1; pnpm install then pnpm dev. Code MIT; many sprites/tiles use CC BY-NC 4.0 and some effect particles have no separate license. Noncommercial fan project; read CREDITS.md.",[4514],{"_841":4515,"_809":4516,"_870":4517},"Play Pokemon Tactics","https://kekel87.itch.io/pokemon-tactics","Author-hosted browser demo on itch.io; choose Run game. Includes AI opponents and hot-seat play. An in-development fan project.",[4519],{"_841":3920,"_809":4507,"_870":-7},[4521,4522,4523,4524],"Play a battle against the built-in opponents and test movement, height, type matchups and friendly fire.","Read the AI disclosure and CREDITS.md before exploring the engine and rendering packages.","Use Node 24 or later and pnpm 10.32.1 to run the complete workspace locally.","Change one tactical rule with an agent, then compare battle resolution, team setup and replay behavior.","The creator directs design and architecture while Claude Code writes most code, tests and documentation with specialist agents. Pokemon data, sprites and some PixelLab artwork have separate credits and rights.","Babylon.js · TypeScript",[4521,4522,4523,4524],{"_841":3920,"_809":4507,"_802":891},{"_841":4515,"_809":4516,"_802":974,"_870":4517},{"_841":1457,"_809":4511,"_870":4512,"_932":933},{"_841":3907,"_809":4507,"_870":4508},[694],"example:clowder-and-crest-agents","Clowder & Crest","Recruit cats into a medieval guild, take jobs across fifteen minigame types, develop bonds and follow a seven-chapter campaign shaped by the guild’s reputation.","/examples/clowder-and-crest-agents/",{"_804":61,"_805":4534,"_807":4535,"_920":1680,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4596,"_901":4597,"_892":4598,"_881":4599,"_816":4600,"_867":4601,"_857":4602,"_1594":4603},[4539,4540,4541,4542,4543,4544,4545,4546,4547,4548,4549,4550,4551,4552,4553,4554,4555,4556,4557,4558],{"_837":805,"_843":4534,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4535,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1680,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4596,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4591,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4588,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4584,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":1592,"_851":4575,"_839":1594,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4570,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4565,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4561,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4560},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":499,"_191":4559,"_193":498,"_816":500,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":501},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/clowder-and-crest-agents.webp",[1190,1650,3533],[4562,4563,4564],{"_841":1194,"_809":1195},{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},{"_841":3533,"_809":3536},[4566],{"_841":4567,"_809":4568,"_870":4569},"Read the creator’s multi-tool attribution","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest#built-with","README names model/tool roles; todo/codex-todo.md and todo/gemini-todo.md are separate development lanes. These are project records rather than a complete prompt transcript.",[4571],{"_841":4572,"_809":4573,"_870":4574},"Open the complete guild-game project","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest","Full Phaser campaign, fifteen minigame types, assets, native shells and tests. Install package dependencies, then npm run dev; the documented dev port is 3200. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.",[4576,4577],{"_841":4581,"_809":4582,"_870":4583},{"_841":4578,"_809":4579,"_870":4580},"GitHub Releases · iOS","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest/releases/tag/v2.7.3","Download — Older v2.7.3 IPA; iOS is not included in v2.8.0. Requires suitable signing and sideloading as described by the author, not direct App Store installation. Not installed in this review.","GitHub Releases · Android","https://github.com/JacobStephens2/clowder-and-crest/releases/tag/v2.8.0","Download — Signed v2.8.0 Android APK for sideloading. This is not a Google Play listing. Installer assets were verified; installation was not tested.",[4585],{"_841":4586,"_809":500,"_870":4587},"Play Clowder & Crest","Browser campaign with mouse/touch minigames. The title screen also offers a spoiler-marked unlocked minigame archive. Android/iOS packaging is included, but native installation has separate platform requirements. Initial asset loading can be slow.",[4589],{"_841":4590,"_809":4568,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s tool and code credits",[4592,4593,4594,4595],"Start a guild and complete an opening job.","Read the tool credits and separate coding lanes.","Inspect one minigame and its dedicated playtest.","Change one job mechanic and check campaign progression and saves.","JacobStephens2 identifies Claude Code as the primary coding and design partner, Codex CLI as a second coding lane, and Gemini CLI as a third. PixelLab, Midjourney, ElevenLabs and Suno supplied different asset types; the repository contains per-agent task files.",[4592,4593,4594,4595],{"_841":4590,"_809":4568,"_802":891},{"_841":4586,"_809":500,"_802":974,"_870":4587},{"_841":4572,"_809":4573,"_932":933,"_870":4574},{"_841":4567,"_809":4568,"_870":4569},[1229,696,706],[4604,4605],{"_1621":4581,"_809":4582,"_802":880,"_870":4607},{"_1621":4578,"_809":4579,"_802":880,"_870":4606},"Older v2.7.3 IPA; iOS is not included in v2.8.0. Requires suitable signing and sideloading as described by the author, not direct App Store installation. Not installed in this review.","Signed v2.8.0 Android APK for sideloading. This is not a Google Play listing. Installer assets were verified; installation was not tested.","example:novel-journey-to-west","Journey to the West: Three Borrowings of the Banana Fan","A Chinese turn-based RPG with painted walking maps, quests, equipment, pets and command battles, adapted from the Banana Fan chapters of Journey to the West.","/examples/novel-journey-to-west/",{"_804":59,"_805":4609,"_807":4610,"_920":4661,"_916":922,"_908":4660,"_901":4662,"_892":4663,"_881":4664,"_816":4665,"_867":4666,"_912":923,"_857":4667},[4614,4615,4616,4617,4618,4619,4620,4621,4622,4623,4624,4625,4626,4627,4628,4629,4630,4631,4632],{"_837":805,"_843":4609,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4610,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4661,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4660,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4655,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4652,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4647,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4642,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4637,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4636},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":504,"_191":4635,"_193":503,"_816":505,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4633},[4634],{"_841":1368,"_809":506},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/novel-journey-to-west.webp",[1779],[4638],{"_841":4639,"_809":4640,"_870":4641},"Read the creator’s workflow and example record","https://github.com/zenstory-ai/novel-to-game#play-online","The creator links the game to the NovelToGame workflow and its adaptation workspace. Published QA is author evidence, not a GameMap reproduction.",[4643],{"_841":4644,"_809":4645,"_870":4646},"Open the complete adaptation and game","https://github.com/zenstory-ai/novel-to-game/tree/main/examples/journey-to-the-west","Includes the static game, painted scene and character assets, design workspace and browser QA. No generation API is required to play the committed build. Repository MIT terms and the source/asset ledgers should be read together.",[4648],{"_841":4649,"_809":4650,"_870":4651},"Play Three Borrowings of the Banana Fan","https://xiyouji.vibecoco.ai/","Chinese-language browser prototype. Click to walk, interact with marked NPCs and choose battle commands. The author records a desktop completion path; narrow-screen play has separate limitations.",[4653],{"_841":4654,"_809":4645,"_870":-7},"Read the adaptation workspace",[4656,4657,4658,4659],"Play the village and use the quest tracker to reach an NPC or a battle.","Compare the novel chapter references with the selected fan, transformation and five-element mechanics.","Read the design, art and QA files to distinguish implemented systems from deliberately omitted multiplayer features.","To run locally, serve examples/journey-to-the-west/build/app with python3 -m http.server 5173; inspect the JavaScript battle implementation before changing a rule.","Zenstory publishes this as a NovelToGame agent-workflow result, with source analysis, rejected concepts, game and art direction, generated artwork, game implementation and QA records. The example does not identify one specific coding client; support for several clients is not proof that all were used.","Custom Canvas 2D · JavaScript · DOM UI",[4656,4657,4658,4659],{"_841":4654,"_809":4645,"_802":1230},{"_841":4649,"_809":4650,"_802":974,"_870":4651},{"_841":4644,"_809":4645,"_870":4646,"_932":933},{"_841":4639,"_809":4640,"_870":4641},[],"example:vibe-racer-opencode","Vibe Racer","A top-down time-trial racer with saved best laps, player and creator ghosts, mud surfaces, and a built-in track editor.","/examples/vibe-racer-opencode/",{"_804":57,"_805":4669,"_807":4670,"_920":4726,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4725,"_901":4727,"_892":4728,"_881":4729,"_816":4730,"_867":4731,"_857":4732},[4674,4675,4676,4677,4678,4679,4680,4681,4682,4683,4684,4685,4686,4687,4688,4689,4690,4691,4692,4693],{"_837":805,"_843":4669,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4670,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4726,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4725,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4720,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4717,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":889,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4712,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4707,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4702,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4699,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4697},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":509,"_191":4696,"_193":508,"_816":510,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4694},[4695],{"_841":1368,"_809":511},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/vibe-racer-opencode.webp",[4698],"OpenCode",[4700],{"_841":4698,"_809":4701},"/resources/opencode/",[4703],{"_841":4704,"_809":4705,"_870":4706},"See OpenCode and model attribution","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer#development","Creator disclosure explicitly names OpenCode and GPT 5.2 Codex. The model name does not imply the Codex coding-agent client was used.",[4708],{"_841":4709,"_809":4710,"_870":4711},"Open the complete racing project","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer","MIT-licensed game source with supplied maps, replays, screenshots, and pyproject.toml/uv.lock. Python 3.12+; the graphical game needs a local desktop display.",[4713],{"_841":4714,"_809":4715,"_870":4716},"Download and run Vibe Racer","https://github.com/Kecksdose/vibe_racer/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","No hosted browser build. Requires Python 3.12+ and Pygame 2.6.1+. Run uv run -m src.main; alternatively pip install -e . then python -m src.main. Arrow keys drive, R restarts, G toggles the ghost, and B returns to track selection. Source-checked launch steps; not executed.",[4718],{"_841":4719,"_809":4705,"_870":-7},"Read the tool and model disclosure",[4721,4722,4723,4724],"Download the source and launch the Pygame window with Python 3.12 or newer.","Race a supplied track and compare the player ghost with the unlockable creator ghost.","Read the development disclosure, then inspect movement, lap timing, and replay storage.","Change a track or handling parameter and complete a validation run before saving.","Kecksdose names OpenCode as the coding tool and GPT 5.2 Codex as the model. The README publishes a short development disclosure, rather than the original prompts or full conversation.","Pygame 2.6 · Python",[4721,4722,4723,4724],{"_841":4719,"_809":4705,"_802":891},{"_841":4714,"_809":4715,"_802":880,"_870":4716},{"_841":4709,"_809":4710,"_932":933,"_870":4711},{"_841":4704,"_809":4705,"_870":4706},[710],"example:golden-hour-skatepark-cursor","Golden Hour Skatepark","Skate an original beachside park: carve transitions, ollie, flip, grind, manual, bail and recover. This complete third-person sandbox has transient trick combos and a changeable time of day, with no levels or persistent score.","/examples/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor/",{"_804":55,"_805":4734,"_807":4735,"_920":4793,"_2871":4794,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":4791,"_901":4795,"_892":4796,"_881":4797,"_816":4798,"_867":4799,"_857":4800},[4739,4740,4741,4742,4743,4744,4745,4746,4747,4748,4749,4750,4751,4752,4753,4754,4755,4756,4757,4758,4759],{"_837":805,"_843":4734,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4735,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4793,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":4792,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4791,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4786,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4782,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4777,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4772,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4767,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4764,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4763},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":514,"_191":4762,"_193":513,"_816":515,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4760},[4761],{"_841":1368,"_809":516},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor.webp",[1257],[4765,4766],{"_841":861,"_809":862},{"_841":2843,"_809":2844},[4768],{"_841":4769,"_809":4770,"_870":4771},"Read the creator’s Cursor contribution account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park#how-it-was-built","The README explicitly names Cursor AI agents and separates builder passes, critic feedback and human playtests; docs/MAKING-OF.md provides a detailed account. Source-checked; performance and playability claims were not reproduced.",[4773],{"_841":4774,"_809":4775,"_870":4776},"Open the complete skating project","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park","Complete TypeScript game, procedural park code, runtime skater/crowd GLBs, textures, audio and source tools. CI uses Node 22 and pnpm 10.18.0; pnpm install then pnpm dev at 127.0.0.1:5188. Ports are fixed. No root LICENSE was found; CC0 media, Mixamo animations and dependencies keep separate terms.",[4778],{"_841":4779,"_809":4780,"_870":4781},"Play Golden Hour Skatepark","https://starknightt.github.io/skate-park/","Browser skating sandbox with keyboard, optional mouse/gamepad and touch controls. Press any key, click or tap to take over from the title-screen rider. Phone testing reported by the creator used desktop emulation; Firefox and desktop Safari remain untested.",[4783],{"_841":4784,"_809":4785,"_870":-7},"Read the builder-and-critic development account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park/blob/main/docs/MAKING-OF.md",[4787,4788,4789,4790],"Play the park and test pushing, carving, one trick, a bail and recovery.","Read the making-of account and separate human feedback, agent implementation and third-party assets.","Use Node 22 with pnpm 10.18.0, then pnpm install and pnpm dev; inspect the collision mesh and character pipeline.","Ask an agent to adjust one movement or camera parameter, then compare transition riding, tricks and recovery across the park.","The author says Cursor AI agents implemented the game through builder and visual-critic passes, with human playtests refining controls. Code-built environments and procedural riding are combined with Cursor-generated artwork, credited CC0 audio/textures and Mixamo recovery animations.",[2843],"Three.js · TypeScript",[2843],[4787,4788,4789,4790],{"_841":4784,"_809":4785,"_802":1230},{"_841":4779,"_809":4780,"_802":974,"_870":4781},{"_841":4774,"_809":4775,"_932":933,"_870":4776},{"_841":4769,"_809":4770,"_870":4771},[931,2881],"example:castle-clash-duel-claude","Castle Clash Duel","Recruit warriors and archers and fight a two-player tactical battle on a tilemap. This complete Phaser prototype pairs Claude Code implementation with Pixel Frog’s Tiny Swords artwork.","/examples/castle-clash-duel-claude/",{"_804":53,"_805":4802,"_807":4803,"_920":2165,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4854,"_901":4855,"_892":4856,"_881":4857,"_816":4858,"_867":4859,"_857":4860},[4807,4808,4809,4810,4811,4812,4813,4814,4815,4816,4817,4818,4819,4820,4821,4822,4823,4824,4825,4826],{"_837":805,"_843":4802,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4803,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":2165,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4854,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4849,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4846,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4841,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4837,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4834,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4831,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4830},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":519,"_191":4829,"_193":518,"_816":520,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4827},[4828],{"_841":1368,"_809":521},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/castle-clash-duel-claude.webp",[1190],[4832,4833],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":1194,"_809":1195},[4835],{"_841":3907,"_809":520,"_870":4836},"README explains PRD-to-code workflow, asset metadata and UI/test implementation; docs/prd.md and docs/tdd.md are published. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[4838],{"_841":1457,"_809":4839,"_870":4840},"https://github.com/chongdashu/phaserjs-tinyswords","Full public/index.html game, Tiny Swords assets, PRD, technical design and UI test harness are included. Open public/index.html in a modern browser. No root LICENSE was found; artwork retains Pixel Frog terms. Do not assume unrestricted reuse.",[4842],{"_841":4843,"_809":4844,"_870":4845},"Play Castle Clash Duel","https://vibe-tiny-swords.vercel.app/","Author-linked browser prototype with mouse or touch controls. The local public/index.html loads Phaser 3.70.0 from a CDN.",[4847],{"_841":4848,"_809":520,"_870":-7},"Read the PRD-to-game workflow",[4850,4851,4852,4853],"Play a two-player battle and identify recruitment, movement, attacks and castle victory conditions.","Read the published PRD and technical design before tracing the game’s single-file scene logic.","Inspect the Tiny Swords asset metadata and the custom panels used to handle sprite padding.","Change one unit or UI rule with an agent, then replay the battle and inspect the included test harness.","The creator combined a PRD, technical design and curated asset metadata with three Claude Code skills for Phaser gameplay, tilemaps and frontend testing. Human-made Tiny Swords assets are credited separately; this is a prototype.",[4850,4851,4852,4853],{"_841":4848,"_809":520,"_802":1230},{"_841":4843,"_809":4844,"_802":974,"_870":4845},{"_841":1457,"_809":4839,"_870":4840,"_932":933},{"_841":3907,"_809":520,"_870":4836},[694,1229],"example:silent-meridian-codex","Silent Meridian","Investigate an observatory trapped at 00:17, compare Present and Echo states, and solve thirteen connected puzzles across four chapters with a journal and optional hints.","/examples/silent-meridian-codex/",{"_804":51,"_805":4862,"_807":4863,"_920":4917,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4916,"_901":4918,"_892":4919,"_881":4920,"_816":4921,"_867":4922,"_857":4923},[4867,4868,4869,4870,4871,4872,4873,4874,4875,4876,4877,4878,4879,4880,4881,4882,4883,4884,4885,4886],{"_837":805,"_843":4862,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4863,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4917,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4916,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4911,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4908,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4903,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4898,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4893,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4891,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4890},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":524,"_191":4889,"_193":523,"_816":525,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":4887},[4888],{"_841":1368,"_809":526},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/silent-meridian-codex.webp",[1650],[4892],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},[4894],{"_841":4895,"_809":4896,"_870":4897},"Read the human and AI contribution record","https://github.com/stackloomdev/silent-meridian/blob/main/docs/CREATION.md","Creator-published model roles, iterative workflow and validation limits. It explicitly describes point-and-click scenes rather than a freely walkable 3D world.",[4899],{"_841":4900,"_809":4901,"_870":4902},"Open the complete puzzle-game project","https://github.com/stackloomdev/silent-meridian","Includes all puzzle logic, chapters, illustrations, local saves, audio, tests and design notes. Node.js 22; npm run dev. No backend, API key, CDN or runtime dependencies.",[4904],{"_841":4905,"_809":4906,"_870":4907},"Play Silent Meridian","https://silent-meridian.pjstack.dev/","English and Chinese; mouse, touch and keyboard. Click objects to investigate; Space changes time, J opens the journal, and Esc closes dialogs. Optional WebGL depth has an illustrated fallback.",[4909],{"_841":4910,"_809":4896,"_870":-7},"Read the creation record",[4912,4913,4914,4915],"Start the opening chapter and compare the two time states.","Read the creation record and art provenance.","Inspect puzzle rules separately from presentation code.","Modify one clue and verify uniqueness, hints and saved progress.","stackloomdev directed iterative GPT-6 Astra work in Codex on story, puzzles, bilingual text, interface, code, saves, procedural WebGL effects and tests. Background illustrations were generated separately; the 3D layer adds depth to point-and-click scenes.","Custom JavaScript · DOM/CSS · WebGL · Web Audio",[4912,4913,4914,4915],{"_841":4910,"_809":4896,"_802":1230},{"_841":4905,"_809":4906,"_802":974,"_870":4907},{"_841":4900,"_809":4901,"_932":933,"_870":4902},{"_841":4895,"_809":4896,"_870":4897},[696],"example:morbreaker-unity-claude","morBreaker","Clear ten brick-breaker levels with a paddle-controlled ball that accelerates on bounces, rising brick durability, and locally saved high scores.","/examples/morbreaker-unity-claude/",{"_804":49,"_805":4925,"_807":4926,"_920":4977,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":4976,"_901":4978,"_892":4979,"_881":4980,"_816":4981,"_867":4982,"_857":4983},[4930,4931,4932,4933,4934,4935,4936,4937,4938,4939,4940,4941,4942,4943,4944,4945,4946,4947,4948],{"_837":805,"_843":4925,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4926,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":4977,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":4976,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":4971,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":4968,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1397,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":4963,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":880,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":4959,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":4954,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":4951,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":4950},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":529,"_191":4949,"_193":528,"_816":530,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":848},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/morbreaker-unity-claude.webp",[1190],[4952,4953],{"_841":3903,"_809":3904},{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},[4955],{"_841":4956,"_809":4957,"_870":4958},"Read the explicit Claude Code contribution breakdown","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker#built-with-claude-code-","Creator disclosure names the Unity MCP package and lists the editor work Claude performed. It is a process summary, not a published prompt transcript.",[4960],{"_841":4961,"_809":530,"_870":4962},"Open the complete Unity game","MIT-licensed Assets, Packages, ProjectSettings, scenes, and C# gameplay source. Requires Unity 6000.4.11f1; open Assets/Scenes/SampleScene.unity and press Play. Windows/WebGL build modules are needed only for packaging; Claude/MCP tooling is not required for play.",[4964],{"_841":4965,"_809":4966,"_870":4967},"Download morBreaker for Windows or WebGL","https://github.com/KingMordas/mor-breaker/releases/tag/v1.2.0","Version 1.2.0 includes Windows standalone and WebGL ZIPs. Extract the Windows build and launch it, or serve the WebGL build over HTTP. A/D or arrows move, Space launches, H shows scores, and Space/Enter restarts. Pointer/touch controls are included; no public hosted play link is supplied.",[4969],{"_841":4970,"_809":4957,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s Unity and Claude Code account",[4972,4973,4974,4975],"Download the Windows release or serve the published WebGL build over HTTP.","Try paddle steering, acceleration, loss, restart, and the local score list.","Read the creator’s Claude Code disclosure and inspect the gameplay C# scripts.","Open SampleScene.unity with Unity 6000.4.11f1, change one level rule, and test progression.","KingMordas says Claude Code built almost the entire game through the Unity MCP plugin: gameplay scripts, scene and prefab wiring, tests, and documentation. The AI editor tooling is separate from the released game runtime.","Unity 6 · URP · C#",[4972,4973,4974,4975],{"_841":4970,"_809":4957,"_802":891},{"_841":4965,"_809":4966,"_802":880,"_870":4967},{"_841":4961,"_809":530,"_932":933,"_870":4962},{"_841":4956,"_809":4957,"_870":4958},[3934,694],"example:deep-yellow-claude","DEEP YELLOW","Explore procedural Backrooms in a first-person, turn-based roguelike. Moving or waiting triggers combat, while equipment combinations and sanity shape each run.","/examples/deep-yellow-claude/",{"_804":47,"_805":4985,"_807":4986,"_920":1612,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":5043,"_901":5044,"_892":5045,"_881":5046,"_816":5047,"_867":5048,"_857":5049,"_1594":5050},[4990,4991,4992,4993,4994,4995,4996,4997,4998,4999,5000,5001,5002,5003,5004,5005,5006,5007,5008,5009,5010],{"_837":805,"_843":4985,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":4986,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1612,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5043,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5038,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5035,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5031,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":1592,"_851":5027,"_839":1594,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5023,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5018,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5015,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5014},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":533,"_191":5013,"_193":532,"_816":534,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":5011},[5012],{"_841":1368,"_809":535},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/deep-yellow-claude.webp",[1190],[5016,5017],{"_841":1448,"_809":1449},{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},[5019],{"_841":5020,"_809":5021,"_870":5022},"Read the explicit Claude Code credit","https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/blob/master/CREDITS.md#code-and-design","Creator attribution specifically names Claude via Claude Code. The itch page separately discloses AI assistance for code; no complete session transcript is supplied.",[5024],{"_841":1524,"_809":5025,"_870":5026},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow","Full Godot 4.6 project, scenes, scripts, assets, shaders, and export presets. The itch page lists code MIT and assets CC0, while CREDITS.md still leaves the original-code license undecided and some third-party licenses unspecified; inspect both before reuse.",[5028],{"_841":1397,"_809":5029,"_870":5030},"https://github.com/aebrer/deep-yellow/releases/tag/v0.13.0","Download — Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.",[5032],{"_841":5033,"_809":534,"_870":5034},"Play DEEP YELLOW","In-development browser build plus Windows/Linux downloads. The creator recommends Chrome or a controller; Firefox mouse input has known problems. Includes horror themes and an interactive tutorial.",[5036],{"_841":5037,"_809":534,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s game and development notes",[5039,5040,5041,5042],"Play the interactive tutorial and compare moving, waiting, equipment, and sanity.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the project’s separate attribution file.","Import project.godot in Godot 4.6 and inspect the start menu, procedural levels, and turn systems.","Change one equipment or turn rule, then test a complete run and restart.","Drew Brereton identifies the game as code-assisted by Claude. The project credits specifically name Claude Code and distinguish original work from external shaders, textures, and fonts.",[5039,5040,5041,5042],{"_841":5037,"_809":534,"_802":1230},{"_841":5033,"_809":534,"_802":974,"_870":5034},{"_841":1524,"_809":5025,"_932":933,"_870":5026},{"_841":5020,"_809":5021,"_870":5022},[1481,694],[5051],{"_1621":1397,"_809":5029,"_802":880,"_870":5052},"Prepared Windows and Linux builds, plus a self-hostable Web export. These are uploaded game builds, separate from automatic source archives. Release files were verified; native builds were not executed.","example:surge-for-oinja-codex","SURGE for Oinja","Shape an electrical build while surviving mechanical swarms across two interactive maps. Automatic attacks leave movement, dodging, upgrades and facility restoration to the player.","/examples/surge-for-oinja-codex/",{"_804":45,"_805":5054,"_807":5055,"_920":5108,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":5107,"_901":5109,"_892":5110,"_881":5111,"_816":5112,"_867":5113,"_85