he creator explicitly says Claude Opus 5.5 generated the code in Claude Cowork. Human planning and publishing are credited separately. Cowork is retained as the actual client rather than being relabelled Claude Code; the conversation itself is not published.","Three.js r169 · JavaScript",[5512,5513,5514,5515],{"_841":5510,"_809":5498,"_802":891},{"_841":5506,"_809":571,"_802":974,"_870":5507},{"_841":1457,"_809":5502,"_932":933,"_870":5503},{"_841":3907,"_809":5498,"_870":5499},[931],"example:clockout-unseen-codex","Clock Out Unseen","Sneak out of three offices before time expires, using furniture, coffee distractions and a temporary folder disguise to avoid patrol sightlines and reach an elevator.","/examples/clockout-unseen-codex/",{"_804":29,"_805":5525,"_807":5526,"_920":5575,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":5574,"_901":5576,"_892":5577,"_881":5578,"_816":5579,"_867":5580,"_857":5581},[5530,5531,5532,5533,5534,5535,5536,5537,5538,5539,5540,5541,5542,5543,5544,5545,5546,5547,5548],{"_837":805,"_843":5525,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5526,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5575,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5574,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5569,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5566,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5562,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5558,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5553,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5551,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5550},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":574,"_191":5549,"_193":573,"_816":575,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/clockout-unseen-codex.webp",[1650],[5552],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},[5554],{"_841":5555,"_809":5556,"_870":5557},"Read the explicit Codex and human contribution account","https://github.com/Ryan-fm/clockout-unseen/blob/main/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md","Creator record names GPT-6 Astra in Codex, gives selected requests and distinguishes independently generated artwork from coding-model work.",[5559],{"_841":1457,"_809":5560,"_870":5561},"https://github.com/Ryan-fm/clockout-unseen","Complete React/Canvas source, maps, original office/character PNGs, tests and Vite configuration. Run npm ci then npm run dev. No runtime AI key. README labels current source V2; verify hosted-version differences before comparing features.",[5563],{"_841":5564,"_809":575,"_870":5565},"Play Clock Out Unseen","Chinese interface on Bilibili Toy. Wait for scene assets, then start a level. WASD/arrows move, E interacts and Space uses a folder disguise; mobile joystick/buttons are supplied. The game opened and started without sign-in.",[5567],{"_841":5568,"_809":5556,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s development record",[5570,5571,5572,5573],"Start Normal mode and move behind office furniture.","Read the selected prompts and model contribution record.","Trace movement, line-of-sight and disguise rules in the engine.","Change one patrol rule and check immediate detection, retry and level progression.","Ryan-fm supplied the office-stealth concept and approved the visual direction. GPT-6 Astra in Codex iterated on collisions, sightlines, patrols, interactions, progression, mobile controls and tests. A separate image-generation tool created office and character art.","Canvas 2D · React UI",[5570,5571,5572,5573],{"_841":5568,"_809":5556,"_802":1230},{"_841":5564,"_809":575,"_802":974,"_870":5565},{"_841":1457,"_809":5560,"_932":933,"_870":5561},{"_841":5555,"_809":5556,"_870":5557},[696],"example:fishslop-claude","Fishslop","Pilot a bathyscaphe through a sunken reef, feed fish, collect the coins they drop and buy new residents or submarine parts. Sonar briefly reveals an otherwise invisible Veilfin.","/examples/fishslop-claude/",{"_804":27,"_805":5583,"_807":5584,"_920":5635,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":5634,"_901":5636,"_892":5637,"_881":5638,"_816":5639,"_867":5640,"_857":5641},[5588,5589,5590,5591,5592,5593,5594,5595,5596,5597,5598,5599,5600,5601,5602,5603,5604,5605,5606],{"_837":805,"_843":5583,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5584,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5635,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5634,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5629,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5625,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":5624,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5620,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5616,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5611,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5609,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5608},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":578,"_191":5607,"_193":577,"_816":579,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/fishslop-claude.webp",[1023],[5610],{"_841":861,"_809":862},[5612],{"_841":5613,"_809":5614,"_870":5615},"Read the initial AI-credited implementation","https://github.com/vasu-devs/FishSlop_Opus5.5/commit/e7a7a2dd61b6da92f9512ccabafad13e1e9a3df4","Initial game implementation explicitly credits Claude Opus 5.5 as co-author; later fix commits repeat that credit. A model credit alone is not attributed to Claude Code.",[5617],{"_841":1457,"_809":5618,"_870":5619},"https://github.com/vasu-devs/FishSlop_Opus5.5","Complete simulation, Three.js renderer, procedural assets, UI, audio, lockfile and tests. npm ci then npm run dev; the README’s Node 20.19+ does not cover every Node 22 version supported by its current Vite 8 dependency, so use Node 22.12+ or another compatible current runtime. No licence file was found; source availability is not a general reuse grant.",[5621],{"_841":5622,"_809":579,"_870":5623},"Play Fishslop","WebGL2 with keyboard, mouse or touch. WASD steers, E/Q changes depth, Space feeds, F pings sonar and B opens the dock. The low-quality preset ?quality=low&scale=0.5 was used to check steering, feeding, coin feedback and sonar.","quickstart",[5626],{"_841":5627,"_809":5628,"_870":-7},"Read the game rules and project structure","https://github.com/vasu-devs/FishSlop_Opus5.5#readme",[5630,5631,5632,5633],"Dive in, steer with WASD, hold Space to feed fish and use F for sonar.","Compare the renderer-free simulation, feeding economy and save parser with the Three.js scene.","Use a Vite-compatible Node runtime, npm ci and npm run dev; Node 22.12+ meets the current Vite 8 requirement.","Change one fish or upgrade value, then check food, dropped coins, dock purchases and saved progress.","The creator’s initial implementation and subsequent fixes explicitly credit Claude Opus 5.5 as a commit co-author. This is evidence of an AI-assisted development contribution; it does not identify the coding client or establish that all code was generated by the model. The reef, fish, textures and sounds are generated by game code.","Three.js · TypeScript · Web Audio",[5630,5631,5632,5633],{"_841":5627,"_809":5628,"_802":5624},{"_841":5622,"_809":579,"_802":974,"_870":5623},{"_841":1457,"_809":5618,"_932":933,"_870":5619},{"_841":5613,"_809":5614,"_870":5615},[931],"example:pelican-bike-claude","Pelican on a Bike","Ride a helmeted pelican along a procedural coast, change lanes to catch fish, jump and unlock small achievements. The complete Three.js project includes its own character, bicycle, ocean, audio and day/night systems.","/examples/pelican-bike-claude/",{"_804":25,"_805":5643,"_807":5644,"_920":1050,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":5692,"_901":5693,"_892":5694,"_881":5695,"_816":5696,"_867":5697,"_857":5698},[5648,5649,5650,5651,5652,5653,5654,5655,5656,5657,5658,5659,5660,5661,5662,5663,5664,5665,5666],{"_837":805,"_843":5643,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5644,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5692,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5687,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5684,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":2219,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5680,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5676,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5672,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5669,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5668},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":582,"_191":5667,"_193":581,"_816":583,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/pelican-bike-claude.webp",[1190],[5670,5671],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":861,"_809":862},[5673],{"_841":3907,"_809":5674,"_870":5675},"https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo#readme","Creator-published prompt and session summary, with exact Claude Code attribution. The model-led long-run tests described there were not repeated by GameMap.",[5677],{"_841":1457,"_809":5678,"_870":5679},"https://github.com/riba2534/claude-opus-5-5-demo/tree/main/pelican-bike","Complete pelican-bike source, build script and procedural assets. Run npm install and node build.mjs in that subdirectory, then open dist/index.html. The repository contains three distinct games; this case selects only the pelican game. Package metadata names ISC, but no repository-wide licence text is supplied.",[5681],{"_841":5682,"_809":583,"_870":5683},"Play Pelican on a Bike","Keyboard and touch controls; W/S accelerate/brake, A/D change lanes, Space jumps and C changes camera. A muted entry is available. Desktop launch, acceleration, jump achievement and camera change were checked.",[5685],{"_841":5686,"_809":5674,"_870":-7},"Read the original prompt and development account",[5688,5689,5690,5691],"Start a muted ride, accelerate with W/S, change lanes with A/D and jump with Space.","Compare the published one-sentence prompt with the pelican, bicycle, cloth, ocean and camera modules.","In pelican-bike, install dependencies and run node build.mjs; open the resulting dist/index.html in a browser.","Change one collection or cycling rule, then check movement, jump, score feedback and restart.","The creator reports generating the game with Claude Opus 5.5 in Claude Code from one Chinese sentence. The README publishes that prompt and describes model-led browser testing and later fixes; the no-manual-code claim is the creator’s, not a measured authorship audit.",[5688,5689,5690,5691],{"_841":5686,"_809":5674,"_802":2219},{"_841":5682,"_809":583,"_802":974,"_870":5683},{"_841":1457,"_809":5678,"_932":933,"_870":5679},{"_841":3907,"_809":5674,"_870":5675},[694,931],"example:three-kingdoms-codex","Three Kingdoms: Hundred Heroes","Manage gold and grain, develop cities and command officers across fifteen strongholds. Choose Wei, Shu or Wu and compete with two computer factions to unify the map.","/examples/three-kingdoms-codex/",{"_804":23,"_805":5700,"_807":5701,"_920":5754,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":5753,"_901":5755,"_892":5756,"_881":5757,"_816":5758,"_867":5759,"_857":5760},[5705,5706,5707,5708,5709,5710,5711,5712,5713,5714,5715,5716,5717,5718,5719,5720,5721,5722,5723,5724],{"_837":805,"_843":5700,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5701,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5754,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5753,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5748,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5745,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5740,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5736,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5731,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5729,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5728},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":586,"_191":5727,"_193":585,"_816":587,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":5725},[5726],{"_841":1368,"_809":588},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/three-kingdoms-codex.webp",[1650],[5730],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},[5732],{"_841":5733,"_809":5734,"_870":5735},"Read the explicit Astra-in-Codex attribution","https://github.com/MartinDelophy/awesome-gpt-6-astra/blob/main/works/three-kingdoms/CREATION.md","The project initiator’s statement distinguishes human direction, Codex implementation and separately generated bitmap assets. It describes multiple iterations rather than one prompt.",[5737],{"_841":1457,"_809":5738,"_870":5739},"https://github.com/MartinDelophy/awesome-gpt-6-astra/tree/main/works/three-kingdoms","Includes rules, interface, 108 officers, generated terrain and portrait atlases, tests and deployment configuration. Node.js 22.13+; npm ci then npm run dev from works/three-kingdoms. Static export uses dist/client. Repository CC0; dependencies retain their own terms.",[5741],{"_841":5742,"_809":5743,"_870":5744},"Play Three Kingdoms","https://sanguo-jiangshan.vercel.app/","Simplified Chinese interface, mouse/touch controls, no login or API key. Choose a faction and start. Saves and JSON import/export are local to the current browser.",[5746],{"_841":5747,"_809":5734,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s contribution record",[5749,5750,5751,5752],"Choose a faction and inspect a city and its officers.","Read the creation record and portrait provenance.","Execute an economic order and follow its resource and officer effects.","Change one economy or combat rule and test turns, opponents and saves.","MartinDelophy supplied the strategy-game direction and requested more officers, portraits and balance changes. GPT-6 Astra in Codex iterated on rules, interface, data, opponents, saves and tests; a separate image tool generated terrain and portrait atlases.","DOM/CSS + SVG · React",[5749,5750,5751,5752],{"_841":5747,"_809":5734,"_802":1230},{"_841":5742,"_809":5743,"_802":974,"_870":5744},{"_841":1457,"_809":5738,"_932":933,"_870":5739},{"_841":5733,"_809":5734,"_870":5735},[696],"example:fang-fox-gbc-claude","Fang the Fox · Game Boy Color","Explore floating islands, fight bosses, solve puzzles and follow a fox’s adventure as a real Game Boy Color game, playable through a browser emulator or a handheld ROM.","/examples/fang-fox-gbc-claude/",{"_804":21,"_805":5762,"_807":5763,"_920":5819,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":5818,"_901":5820,"_892":5821,"_881":5822,"_816":5823,"_867":5824,"_857":5825,"_1594":5826},[5767,5768,5769,5770,5771,5772,5773,5774,5775,5776,5777,5778,5779,5780,5781,5782,5783,5784,5785,5786],{"_837":805,"_843":5762,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5763,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5819,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5818,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5813,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5810,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5806,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":1592,"_851":5801,"_839":1594,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5796,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5791,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5790},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":591,"_191":5789,"_193":590,"_816":592,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":5787},[5788],{"_841":1368,"_809":593},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/fang-fox-gbc-claude.webp",[1190],[5792],{"_841":5793,"_809":5794,"_870":5795},"Read the explicit Claude Code and Opus credit","https://tinybitadventures.com/fang-the-fox-on-the-game-boy-color/","First-person creator account names Claude Code with Opus 5.5 and distinguishes generated implementation from the creator’s direction and music listening. Reported automated test totals were not independently reproduced.",[5797],{"_841":5798,"_809":5799,"_870":5800},"Open the complete cartridge and browser project","https://github.com/TinyBitAdventures/fang-the-fox","The gbc/ C project, generators, music arrangements and web emulator are public. Download the whole repository: gbc/tools/build.js reads ../js data and sprites. Rebuilding requires Node and GBDK-2020 4.5.0; the ready-made ROM needs neither. Code/pixel art are MIT; music is excluded from that license.",[5802],{"_841":5803,"_809":5804,"_870":5805},"GitHub Releases · GBC","https://github.com/TinyBitAdventures/fang-the-fox/releases/tag/gbc-v1.0.0","Download — Game Boy Color ROM and GBC release ZIP. Requires a compatible emulator or cartridge device; the ROM was not executed in this review.",[5807],{"_841":5808,"_809":592,"_870":5809},"Play Fang the Fox for Game Boy Color","Click Start game, focus the emulator, then press Enter/X to start. Arrow keys move, attack and talk; X is A, Z is B, Enter pauses, and Shift shows the area. Hold keys briefly across emulator frames. The page also offers a 256 KB .gbc ROM for compatible emulators or hardware.",[5811],{"_841":5812,"_809":5794,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s Game Boy porting account",[5814,5815,5816,5817],"Start the browser emulator, choose New Game and advance the opening dialogue with X.","Move, interact and inspect the pause map before comparing the cartridge edition with the original browser game.","Read the creator’s porting account and the C implementation under gbc/src/.","Clone the whole repository, then use Node and GBDK-2020 4.5.0 to rebuild through gbc/Makefile; the generator also reads the root JavaScript game data.","Austin Ginder says Claude Code running Opus 5.5 ported his browser game to C. The creator provided direction and listened to the adapted music; the public build tools share maps, sprites and rules between the original and the cartridge version.","GBDK-2020 4.5 · C / hUGEDriver",[5814,5815,5816,5817],{"_841":5812,"_809":5794,"_802":1230},{"_841":5808,"_809":592,"_802":974,"_870":5809},{"_841":5798,"_809":5799,"_932":933,"_870":5800},{"_841":5793,"_809":5794,"_870":5795},[],[5827],{"_1621":5803,"_809":5804,"_802":880,"_870":5828},"Game Boy Color ROM and GBC release ZIP. Requires a compatible emulator or cartridge device; the ROM was not executed in this review.","example:vibe-golf-bevy","Vibe Golf","Charge and release shots across a hilly, prop-filled 3D landscape while chasing moving duck targets in a small arcade golf sandbox.","/examples/vibe-golf-bevy/",{"_804":19,"_805":5830,"_807":5831,"_920":5878,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":5877,"_901":5879,"_892":5880,"_881":5881,"_816":5882,"_867":5883,"_857":5884},[5835,5836,5837,5838,5839,5840,5841,5842,5843,5844,5845,5846,5847,5848,5849,5850,5851,5852],{"_837":805,"_843":5830,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5831,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5878,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5877,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5872,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5869,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5865,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5860,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5855,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5854},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":596,"_191":5853,"_193":595,"_816":597,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/vibe-golf-bevy.webp",[1779],[5856],{"_841":5857,"_809":5858,"_870":5859},"Read the human and GPT-5 contribution statement","https://www.reddit.com/r/ChatGPT/comments/1mnllsq/vibe_coded_a_3d_game_with_gpt_5_and_rust/","First-person creator post links both this source and live build, distinguishes the heightmap from generated assets and describes iterative direction. It does not establish use of Codex or another named coding client.",[5861],{"_841":5862,"_809":5863,"_870":5864},"Open the complete Bevy game","https://github.com/ahammer/vibe_golf","Rust game, Cargo setup, terrain/shaders, audio, GLB props and a prebuilt web/ WASM version are public. Cargo.toml uses Bevy0.14 and Rapier0.27; cargo run launches native play. Asset-heavy repository; code license is marked TBD and asset terms are not consolidated.",[5866],{"_841":5867,"_809":597,"_870":5868},"Play Vibe Golf","Small experimental browser golf sandbox. Initial WASM and asset loading can be slow; use a GPU-capable desktop Chrome browser. Click Play, hold/release left mouse to shoot, right-drag to orbit and scroll to zoom. The game currently logs missing optional .meta requests even though the corresponding assets load.",[5870],{"_841":5871,"_809":5858,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s GPT-5 development account",[5873,5874,5875,5876],"Wait for the browser build to render, then click Play in the middle of the canvas.","Hold and release the left mouse button to launch the ball; use right-drag to orbit and the wheel to zoom.","Read the creator’s account and compare source plugins for terrain, shooting, physics and game state.","Use a local Rust toolchain to run cargo run, change one shot parameter and test launch, movement and target progression.","The creator describes almost all development and generated assets as a GPT-5 experiment, with the preferred heightmap supplied separately and repeated human design changes. The exact coding client is not identified; the project includes its gameplay and rendering source rather than only a model prompt.","Bevy 0.14 + Rapier 0.27 · Rust / WebAssembly",[5873,5874,5875,5876],{"_841":5871,"_809":5858,"_802":891},{"_841":5867,"_809":597,"_802":974,"_870":5868},{"_841":5862,"_809":5863,"_932":933,"_870":5864},{"_841":5857,"_809":5858,"_870":5859},[],"example:core-business-claude","Core Business","Drill for minerals, manage fuel and hull condition, and spend earnings at surface shops in a non-commercial mining tech demo inspired by Motherload. Three.js renders the 2.5D world while Blender scripts produce its 3D assets.","/examples/core-business-claude/",{"_804":17,"_805":5886,"_807":5887,"_920":1050,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":5936,"_901":5938,"_892":5939,"_881":5940,"_816":5941,"_867":5942,"_857":5943,"_2871":5944},[5891,5892,5893,5894,5895,5896,5897,5898,5899,5900,5901,5902,5903,5904,5905,5906,5907,5908,5909,5910],{"_837":805,"_843":5886,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5887,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":1050,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":5937,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5936,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5931,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5928,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5924,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5920,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5916,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5913,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5912},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":600,"_191":5911,"_193":599,"_816":601,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/core-business-claude.webp",[1023],[5914,5915],{"_841":861,"_809":862},{"_841":2843,"_809":2844},[5917],{"_841":3907,"_809":5918,"_870":5919},"https://github.com/Leichtbier/core-business#readme","The author explicitly separates Claude-generated work from ElevenLabs audio and credits Motherload/XGen Studios. This does not imply that Claude created the original game’s rules.",[5921],{"_841":1457,"_809":5922,"_870":5923},"https://github.com/Leichtbier/core-business","Complete JavaScript game, vendored Three.js, committed GLBs, Blender source scripts, UI, audio and tests. Serve the root, e.g. python3 -m http.server 5173; Blender regeneration is unnecessary for normal play. Code is MIT with explicit exceptions: ElevenLabs audio is supplied for this project, not separate extraction or redistribution; see LICENSE.",[5925],{"_841":5926,"_809":601,"_870":5927},"Play Core Business","WebGL browser, keyboard/pointer and touch controls. Initial graphics preparation stalled with the default headless renderer; Chrome with Metal reached normal play. After the opening transmission, brief movement/drilling input produced score 25 and fuel/depth feedback. Full mining progression and audio were not tested.",[5929],{"_841":5930,"_809":5918,"_870":-7},"Read the mining game’s implementation and asset pipeline",[5932,5933,5934,5935],"Start a new game and learn movement, downward drilling, fuel and return-to-surface shops.","Read the fixed-step simulation separately from the Three.js renderer and committed GLB models.","Serve the repository root with a static HTTP server; opening ES modules via file:// does not work.","Change one mineral or upgrade rule, then check drilling, selling, fuel use and save/reload.","The creator attributes the game code, tests, textures, translations, models and Blender generation scripts to Claude Opus 5.5. ElevenLabs supplied the sound and music. The project reimplements Motherload-style rules with new assets and explicitly describes itself as a non-commercial experiment; the coding client is not named.",[2843,3432],[5932,5933,5934,5935],{"_841":5930,"_809":5918,"_802":1230},{"_841":5926,"_809":601,"_802":974,"_870":5927},{"_841":1457,"_809":5922,"_932":933,"_870":5923},{"_841":3907,"_809":5918,"_870":5919},[931,2881],[2843,3432],"example:eight-second-crew-codex","8-Second Crew · 8초 도둑단","Record an eight-second route, replay it as a clone and cooperate with earlier selves to steal a key and escape. Nine stages introduce pressure plates, patrols and projectiles.","/examples/eight-second-crew-codex/",{"_804":15,"_805":5946,"_807":5947,"_920":5399,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":5996,"_901":5999,"_892":6000,"_881":6001,"_816":6002,"_867":6003,"_857":6004,"_2871":6005},[5951,5952,5953,5954,5955,5956,5957,5958,5959,5960,5961,5962,5963,5964,5965,5966,5967,5968,5969,5970],{"_837":805,"_843":5946,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":5947,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5399,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":5997,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":5996,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":5991,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":5988,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":979,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":5984,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":5980,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":5975,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":5973,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":5972},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":604,"_191":5971,"_193":603,"_816":605,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/eight-second-crew-codex.webp",[1650],[5974],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},[5976],{"_841":5977,"_809":5978,"_870":5979},"Read the author’s human and Codex division of work","https://github.com/sdj3261/openai_game_2026#codex와-함께-만든-과정","README and the creator’s linked article describe concrete planning, implementation, sprite, QA and deployment work; neither is a complete session transcript.",[5981],{"_841":1457,"_809":5982,"_870":5983},"https://github.com/sdj3261/openai_game_2026","Complete static project with modules, nine stages, sprites, fonts, tests and demo recording. Node.js 18+; npm start, with no dependency installation. Code has no explicit license; the bundled Galmuri font uses OFL.",[5985],{"_841":5986,"_809":605,"_870":5987},"Play 8-Second Crew","Korean, English and Japanese; keyboard, click-to-move and touch. WASD/arrows move, X records a clone, Z lures guards, and R restarts. Wait through the brief Ready countdown before moving.",[5989],{"_841":5990,"_809":5978,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s Codex build account",[5992,5993,5994,5995],"Start the first stage and learn movement, keys and exits.","Read the creator’s Codex development account and asset credits.","Press X to record a route, then inspect how the clone replays it.","Change a stage or replay rule and test a complete escape and restart.","DongJae Shin set the rules, difficulty and presentation, while Codex helped plan and implement stages, collision, replay, interface, tests and deployment. Agent Sprite Forge processed generated character sprites; the creator repeatedly playtested the result.",[5998],"Agent Sprite Forge",[5992,5993,5994,5995],{"_841":5990,"_809":5978,"_802":1230},{"_841":5986,"_809":605,"_802":974,"_870":5987},{"_841":1457,"_809":5982,"_932":933,"_870":5983},{"_841":5977,"_809":5978,"_870":5979},[696],[5998],"example:word-rain-chatgpt","Word Rain","Move a basket to catch letters in the right order, complete shuffled words and survive red hazards. Shields, wildcards, perfect-word streaks and changing falling speed add decisions to the arcade spelling loop.","/examples/word-rain-chatgpt/",{"_804":163,"_805":6007,"_807":6008,"_920":6067,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":6066,"_901":6068,"_892":6069,"_881":6070,"_816":6071,"_867":6072,"_857":6073,"_1594":6074},[6012,6013,6014,6015,6016,6017,6018,6019,6020,6021,6022,6023,6024,6025,6026,6027,6028,6029,6030,6031],{"_837":805,"_843":6007,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6008,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":6067,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":6066,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":6061,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":6057,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":5624,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":6053,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":1592,"_851":6046,"_839":1594,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":6041,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":6036,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":6034,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":6033},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":263,"_191":6032,"_193":262,"_816":264,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/word-rain-chatgpt.webp",[1578,1650],[6035],{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},[6037],{"_841":6038,"_809":6039,"_870":6040},"Read the author’s ChatGPT/Codex disclosure","https://octopuskid.itch.io/word-rain","The author explicitly credits ChatGPT/Codex for code and interface text, retaining design and refinement. The repository also links a behind-the-scenes development video. No exact model version is specified.",[6042],{"_841":6043,"_809":6044,"_870":6045},"Open the complete browser and Android project","https://github.com/octopuskid/word-rain","Complete index.html, game handwriting font, bundled recordings and audio credits, plus Android Java/WebView source and packaging scripts. Open the HTML with assets/music intact; the original generated tune works without those two recordings. Code, original font, tune and synthesized effects are MIT; Kevin MacLeod recordings are CC BY 4.0. See android/README.md for Android builds.",[6047,6048],{"_841":6051,"_809":264,"_870":6052},{"_841":1397,"_809":6049,"_870":6050},"https://github.com/octopuskid/word-rain/releases/tag/v1.5.3","Download — Version 1.5.3, published 19 October 2026: Full/Lite Android APKs, self-contained Lite HTML/ZIP and the complete offline browser ZIP. Android requires 8.0+. Release page and Lite APK/ZIP HTTP endpoints returned 200; installation was not tested.","GitHub Pages","Browser play — Alternative author-hosted browser edition; normal start, moving letters and direction-key basket controls were checked.",[6054],{"_841":6055,"_809":6039,"_870":6056},"Play Word Rain on itch.io","Free browser game with keyboard, drag and touch controls; an alternative browser build is linked on GitHub Pages. The store and GitHub Releases also offer Full/Lite Android APKs and an offline Lite HTML ZIP. Android requires 8.0+. Browser start, moving letters and basket controls were checked; APK installation and a complete scoring run were not tested.",[6058],{"_841":6059,"_809":6060,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s source and run guide","https://github.com/octopuskid/word-rain#run-the-game",[6062,6063,6064,6065],"Start the browser game and move the basket with the arrow keys, A/D or pointer dragging.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and compare the browser and Android editions.","Open index.html with the bundled assets/music directory, or use the self-contained Lite download for offline browser play.","Trace letter spawning, catches, shields and score updates in the Canvas game; check pause and resume before changing a rule.","octopuskid designed and refined the game, while ChatGPT/Codex assisted with code and interface text. The original tune and sound effects are synthesized in code with ChatGPT assistance. Two optional Kevin MacLeod recordings have separate credits; they are not AI-generated music.","Canvas 2D · JavaScript · DOM/CSS UI",[6062,6063,6064,6065],{"_841":6059,"_809":6060,"_802":5624},{"_841":6055,"_809":6039,"_802":974,"_870":6056},{"_841":6043,"_809":6044,"_932":933,"_870":6045},{"_841":6038,"_809":6039,"_870":6040},[696],[6075,6076],{"_1621":6051,"_809":264,"_802":974,"_870":6078},{"_1621":1397,"_809":6049,"_802":880,"_870":6077},"Version 1.5.3, published 19 October 2026: Full/Lite Android APKs, self-contained Lite HTML/ZIP and the complete offline browser ZIP. Android requires 8.0+. Release page and Lite APK/ZIP HTTP endpoints returned 200; installation was not tested.","Alternative author-hosted browser edition; normal start, moving letters and direction-key basket controls were checked.","example:minimal-rogue-claude","Minimal Rogue","Explore a monochrome dungeon, break blocks, manage stamina and equipment, and descend through an ASCII-style roguelike with English and Japanese interfaces.","/examples/minimal-rogue-claude/",{"_804":167,"_805":6080,"_807":6081,"_920":5399,"_916":922,"_912":1743,"_908":6128,"_901":6129,"_892":6130,"_881":6131,"_816":6132,"_867":6133,"_857":6134},[6085,6086,6087,6088,6089,6090,6091,6092,6093,6094,6095,6096,6097,6098,6099,6100,6101,6102,6103],{"_837":805,"_843":6080,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6081,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":5399,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":1742,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":6128,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":6123,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":6120,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":891,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":6116,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":6112,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":6108,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":6106,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":6105},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":254,"_191":6104,"_193":253,"_816":255,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/minimal-rogue-claude.webp",[1190],[6107],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},[6109],{"_841":6110,"_809":255,"_870":6111},"Read the author’s Claude Code and SUNO attribution","The creator identifies Claude Code for development, SUNO AI for music, links the complete repository and explicitly describes the work as created entirely using AI. No model version or full development transcript is supplied.",[6113],{"_841":1457,"_809":6114,"_870":6115},"https://github.com/HirotakaAdachi/Rogue/tree/anonymous-release","Complete static HTML/CSS/JavaScript project and four MP3 tracks; serve the root over HTTP without a package install or build step. MIT code license is included; SUNO music is credited without a separate music license. The reviewed public source index references script version 549, while the itch build references 581, so the two releases are not claimed to be byte-identical.",[6117],{"_841":6118,"_809":255,"_870":6119},"Play Minimal Rogue on itch.io","Browser keyboard game. Enter confirms the opening and tutorial; arrows move, Space defends, and X opens the menu. A short first-floor run verified movement, block-cracking feedback and the command menu. Later floors, saves and a complete run were not tested.",[6121],{"_841":6122,"_809":255,"_870":-7},"Read the creator’s AI and source-code notes",[6124,6125,6126,6127],"Run the browser game, choose a new game and language, and confirm the opening and tutorial with Enter.","Use the arrow keys to explore the first room, Space to defend and X to open the command menu.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and inspect the complete HTML, CSS, JavaScript and music files.","Serve the source folder over HTTP, change one room or stamina rule, and check movement, interactions and a new run.","Hirotaka Adachi names Claude Code as the development tool and SUNO AI for music, and describes the work as entirely AI-created. The exact coding model is not identified. The public project contains the game renderer, rules, interface and four music files; the creator’s claim does not establish autonomous development without human direction.",[6124,6125,6126,6127],{"_841":6122,"_809":255,"_802":891},{"_841":6118,"_809":255,"_802":974,"_870":6119},{"_841":1457,"_809":6114,"_932":933,"_870":6115},{"_841":6110,"_809":255,"_870":6111},[694],"example:polar-icecapade-claude","Polar Icecapade","Slide across icy 3D arenas, use a three-hit melee combo to propel yourself forward, and fire projectiles that push you backward. Open gates and collect coins while confronting a rat regime in a short game-jam adventure.","/examples/polar-icecapade-claude/",{"_804":171,"_805":6136,"_807":6137,"_920":6191,"_916":1051,"_912":923,"_908":6187,"_2871":6192,"_901":6193,"_892":6194,"_881":6195,"_816":6196,"_867":6197,"_857":6198},[6141,6142,6143,6144,6145,6146,6147,6148,6149,6150,6151,6152,6153,6154,6155,6156,6157,6158,6159,6160],{"_837":805,"_843":6136,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6137,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":6191,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":6188,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":1049,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":6187,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":6182,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":6179,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":6175,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":6171,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":6167,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":6163,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":6162},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":239,"_191":6161,"_193":238,"_816":240,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":960},{"_837":838,"_839":840,"_841":842,"_843":243},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/polar-icecapade-claude.webp",[1190],[6164,6165,6166],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":1448,"_809":1449},{"_841":2843,"_809":2844},[6168],{"_841":6169,"_809":240,"_870":6170},"Read the team’s explicit Claude Code assistance statement","The creators distinguish AI help with diagnosing and implementing core code from their own code review, modeling, animation and art. The page links the full game source and identifies Godot 4.6 and GDScript; its “No generative AI” content badge does not erase the separate coding-assistance disclosure.",[6172],{"_841":3411,"_809":6173,"_870":6174},"https://github.com/afenkurtz/Big-Mode-Game-Jam-2026/tree/main/slick","Complete Godot 4.6 project with levels, GDScript, GLB/FBX models, Blender authoring files, textures, UI and audio. The inspected tree has 292 files, about 239 MB. Open the slick folder; importing Blender authoring files may require a compatible Blender installation. No top-level game license was found; external sounds, music and fonts retain their separately credited terms.",[6176],{"_841":6177,"_809":240,"_870":6178},"Play or download Polar Icecapade on itch.io","Mouse recommended: left-click performs melee propulsion, right-click shoots with recoil, and Escape pauses. Browser review reached the first level, moved, fired a projectile with ammo changing from 12 to 11, and opened pause. The roughly 170 MB web build has author-documented performance limits; Windows/Linux downloads are provided and mobile is not recommended. Later levels and a complete run were not tested.",[6180],{"_841":6181,"_809":240,"_870":-7},"Read the team’s development and asset breakdown",[6183,6184,6185,6186],"Start the first browser level with a mouse and test the slippery movement and melee combo.","Use right-click shooting and compare its backward recoil with forward melee propulsion.","Read the team’s Claude Code disclosure and human art, animation and audio credits.","Open the slick project folder in Godot 4.6, change one movement or gate rule, and test the first room, ammo and pause/restart controls.","Aidan “Botodo” Connolly and Evan Kurtz describe Claude Code helping diagnose problems and implement difficult core logic; they then touched and tweaked all code. They modeled, rigged, animated and designed the game themselves, using credited external audio. They explicitly state that generative AI was not used to create assets. No coding model version is supplied.",[2843,6189,6190],"Procreate","Affinity","Godot 4.6 · GDScript · 3D",[2843,6189,6190],[6183,6184,6185,6186],{"_841":6181,"_809":240,"_802":1230},{"_841":6177,"_809":240,"_802":974,"_870":6178},{"_841":3411,"_809":6173,"_932":933,"_870":6174},{"_841":6169,"_809":240,"_870":6170},[694,1481,2881],"example:overexposed-ai","Overexposed","Guide a rising performer through a year of career choices in a card-based fame simulation. Play cards to build craft, money and attention while three newspapers react and excessive heat turns into scandals.","/examples/overexposed-ai/",{"_804":165,"_805":6200,"_807":6201,"_920":6258,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":6255,"_901":6259,"_892":6260,"_881":6261,"_816":6262,"_867":6263,"_857":6264,"_2871":6265},[6205,6206,6207,6208,6209,6210,6211,6212,6213,6214,6215,6216,6217,6218,6219,6220,6221,6222,6223,6224,6225],{"_837":805,"_843":6200,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6201,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":6258,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":6256,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":6255,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":6250,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":6246,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":5624,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":6242,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":6237,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":6233,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":6230,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":6229},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":258,"_191":6228,"_193":257,"_816":259,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":6226},[6227],{"_841":1368,"_809":260},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/overexposed-ai.webp",[1190,1650],[6231,6232],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":1655,"_809":1656},[6234],{"_841":6235,"_809":259,"_870":6236},"Read the creator’s AI contribution and asset disclosure","The author names Claude Code and OpenAI Codex and explains human editing of text. README confirms AI-assisted commits with Co-Authored-By trailers; CREDITS.md explains procedural pictures/effects and the separate music/font sources.",[6238],{"_841":6239,"_809":6240,"_870":6241},"Open the complete career-simulation project","https://github.com/zsh56609/overexposed","Complete TypeScript/React project with the rule engine, content, UI drawings, procedural sound, six music files, fonts, balance simulator and browser checks. Node.js >=22.18; npm install, npm run dev or npm run build. No explicit software license is provided, so public source availability does not establish reuse rights. Bundled fonts are OFL 1.1 and Holizna music is CC0; see CREDITS.md.",[6243],{"_841":6244,"_809":259,"_870":6245},"Play Overexposed on itch.io","Browser playtest build, best on a landscape desktop screen. Uses mouse or touch; cards show effects on hover or long press. Begin, opening text and manager choice reached the live card desk in Chrome. The complete year, all endings and touch play were not tested; the hosted build is not claimed to match the latest repository revision.",[6247],{"_841":6248,"_809":6249,"_870":-7},"Read the game’s source and local run commands","https://github.com/zsh56609/overexposed#readme",[6251,6252,6253,6254],"Open the itch.io browser build, choose Begin and Continue, then sign with a manager.","Select an opening card offer and inspect how the desk, resources and newspapers respond.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure, README and CREDITS.md to separate code-generated art and effects from third-party music.","Use Node.js 22.18+ with npm install and npm run dev; trace content/cards.json through core/reducer.ts and the React desk before testing a complete year.","EG30 provides design, direction and writing, using Claude Code and OpenAI Codex for implementation. AI-assisted drafts of player text are edited by the creator. Art and sound effects are drawn or synthesized in code with AI assistance; the Holizna background recordings are separately credited CC0 music.",[6257],"Canvas 2D (procedural halftone art)","DOM/CSS + SVG · React UI",[6251,6252,6253,6254],{"_841":6248,"_809":6249,"_802":5624},{"_841":6244,"_809":259,"_802":974,"_870":6245},{"_841":6239,"_809":6240,"_932":933,"_870":6241},{"_841":6235,"_809":259,"_870":6236},[694,696],[6257],"example:katana-kitsune-godot","Katana Kitsune: Prototype","Choose a kitsune fighter and face yokai in an isometric action roguelike with katana combat, stamina, pickups and successive dungeon floors. The silent prototype supports local multiplayer, with additional party systems documented in the current source.","/examples/katana-kitsune-godot/",{"_804":169,"_805":6267,"_807":6268,"_920":6333,"_916":922,"_912":923,"_908":6327,"_2871":6334,"_901":6335,"_892":6336,"_881":6337,"_816":6338,"_867":6339,"_857":6340},[6272,6273,6274,6275,6276,6277,6278,6279,6280,6281,6282,6283,6284,6285,6286,6287,6288,6289,6290,6291,6292],{"_837":805,"_843":6267,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6268,"_839":807,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":918,"_843":6333,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":2868,"_898":2869,"_851":6328,"_839":2871,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":914,"_843":915,"_839":916,"_858":917},{"_837":838,"_841":910,"_843":911,"_839":912,"_858":913},{"_837":838,"_841":906,"_843":6327,"_839":908,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":897,"_898":899,"_851":6322,"_839":901,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":893,"_851":6318,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":890,"_843":1211,"_839":892,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":888,"_843":1794,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":882,"_851":6314,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":879,"_843":974,"_839":881,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":874,"_851":6310,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":872,"_843":873,"_839":816,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":865,"_851":6305,"_839":867,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":855,"_851":6297,"_839":857,"_858":-7},{"_837":849,"_839":11,"_841":850,"_851":6296},{"_837":844,"_839":845,"_841":246,"_191":6295,"_193":245,"_816":247,"_201":202,"_203":204,"_847":1374},{"_837":838,"_839":1371,"_841":1372,"_843":243},{"_837":854,"_839":1367,"_841":1368,"_851":6293},[6294],{"_841":1368,"_809":249},"/GameMap/assets/media/learning/katana-kitsune-godot.webp",[1190,1376],[6298,6299,6300,6301,6302],{"_841":1190,"_809":1196},{"_841":1448,"_809":1449},{"_841":1717,"_809":1718},{"_841":6303,"_809":6304},{"_841":2843,"_809":2844},"Meshy API","/resources/meshy/",[6306],{"_841":6307,"_809":6308,"_870":6309},"Read the creator’s AI production disclosure","https://9-k9.itch.io/katanakitsune","The author explicitly names Claude Code and GitHub Copilot alongside image, sprite and 3D asset tools, and links the primary complete source repository. The README verifies the Godot version and explains which finished assets are included.",[6311],{"_841":3411,"_809":6312,"_870":6313},"https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune","Godot 4.7 project with scenes, GDScript, Dialogic addon and finished sprite assets. The inspected tree contains about 383 MB of files; no top-level game license was found. The upstream Meshy/Blender/PixelOver authoring pipeline is separate, while its finished runtime sprites are committed. The current source contains newer party/asset changes than the reviewed hosted prototype.",[6315],{"_841":6316,"_809":6308,"_870":6317},"Play Katana Kitsune on itch.io","Silent HTML5 prototype with keyboard and gamepad support. Space confirms player/device choices; allow a clear press and release between setup steps. The browser build loaded and reached player/device selection in review; combat and a complete dungeon run were not exercised. The download is large: about 184 MB of game data plus 40 MB of WebAssembly.",[6319],{"_841":6320,"_809":6321,"_870":-7},"Read the game and asset-pipeline documentation","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune#readme",[6323,6324,6325,6326],"Open the itch prototype and choose one human player, then claim a keyboard and select a costume.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the repository’s character, combat and sprite-pipeline notes.","Open project.godot in Godot 4.7 using GL Compatibility; the finished sprites and game scenes are included.","Change one combat or spawn setting, then check the title-to-character-to-dungeon flow, damage and restart.","The creator identifies Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, GPT Image 2, PixelLab and Meshy among the production tools. The repository documents Meshy rigs and animation, Blender retargeting and PixelOver sprite exports. The exact coding models and division of code between assistants are not specified; generated NPC teammates are not the evidence for AI-assisted development.",[6329,6330,6331,2843,6332],"GPT Image 2","PixelLab","Meshy","PixelOver","Godot 4.7 · GDScript · 2D / GL Compatibility",[6329,6330,6331,2843,6332],[6323,6324,6325,6326],{"_841":6320,"_809":6321,"_802":1230},{"_841":6316,"_809":6308,"_802":974,"_870":6317},{"_841":3411,"_809":6312,"_932":933,"_870":6313},{"_841":6307,"_809":6308,"_870":6309}