havior. It exposes the actual edit blocks and applied Git commits, making the incremental coding workflow inspectable rather than presenting an unexplained final screenshot.","/agents/aider-pong-game-editing-transcript/","/agents/",{"_804":6375,"_805":6376,"_802":6435,"_3":6436,"_920":6429,"_6434":6377,"_197":6427,"_6421":6423,"_6416":6418,"_6410":6409,"_6407":6406,"_6401":899,"_6413":6437,"_6404":6403,"_6398":200},[6383,6384,6385,6386,6387,6388,6389,6390,6391,6392,6393,6394,6395,6396],"website/src/data/agentGameResources.ts",{"_837":805,"_843":6376,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6377,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6433,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6431,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6429,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6425,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6420,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6415,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6412,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6409,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6406,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6403,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6400,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"Source reviewed","reviewed","Source classification","Publisher / maintainer source","official","Publisher","Aider","publisher","Limitations","Historical documentation examples, not a separately packaged current game repository or benchmark. Reconstruct the applied edits and install pygame to run Pong; no current model-performance claim is implied. The original 2048 game is human-authored and is only used to demonstrate an AI-assisted modification.","limitations","What the source actually contains","Published transcript with Python edit blocks for pong_game.py, Paddle/Ball classes, input, collision, drawing, ball reset, and customizations. Numeric score display is suggested rather than implemented in this transcript. The related 2048 transcript shows inspecting js/game_manager.js and patching its scoring logic in an existing public JavaScript game.","codeScope","Code type","Instructions","codeType","Evidence",[6417],"evidenceUrl",{"_841":6414,"_809":6418},"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/blob/main/aider/website/examples/2048-game.md","Code / instructions",[6422],"codeUrl",{"_841":6419,"_809":6423},"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/blob/main/aider/website/examples/pong.md","Primary source",[6426],{"_841":6424,"_809":6427},"https://aider.chat/examples/pong.html","Engine / runtime","pygame · Python","Attributed clients / models",[6403],"Toolkit category","Build workflows","summary","workflow",[6438],"instructions","aider","agent:gamedev-agent-skills-router","gamedev-agent-skills-router","GameDev Agent Skills: engine router and test/code recipes","A community skill library whose router detects the project’s engine and loads task-specific guidance. Beyond a directory of links, it contains the actual skill bodies, source-backed code recipes, a skill validator, and asset-report/preview utilities.","/agents/gamedev-agent-skills-router/",{"_804":6440,"_805":6441,"_802":6477,"_3":6478,"_920":6473,"_6434":6442,"_197":6472,"_6421":6469,"_6416":6466,"_6410":6463,"_6407":6462,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6437,"_6404":6461,"_6398":200},[6446,6447,6448,6449,6450,6451,6452,6453,6454,6455,6456,6457,6458,6459],{"_837":805,"_843":6441,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6442,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6476,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6474,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6473,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6470,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6467,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6464,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6412,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6463,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6462,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6461,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"Third-party / community source","gamedev-skills","Primarily a version-targeted instruction/example library rather than an engine-control runtime. Current Godot testing guidance targets 4.7; other engine groups have their own baselines. Install compatibility statements are the maintainer’s claims, and this research did not execute cross-agent smoke tests.","Router and engine/discipline/genre/workflow SKILL.md files. Verified skills/godot/godot-gdscript-headless-testing/SKILL.md contains a SceneTree test-runner recipe and explicit failure exit handling; scripts/validate-skills.py validates the collection; skills/disciplines/create-game-assets/scripts/ includes asset_report.py and build_preview_sheet.py. README names native Gemini CLI support.",[6465],{"_841":6414,"_809":6466},"https://github.com/gamedev-skills/awesome-gamedev-agent-skills/blob/main/router/SKILL.md",[6468],{"_841":6419,"_809":6469},"https://github.com/gamedev-skills/awesome-gamedev-agent-skills/tree/main/skills",[6471],{"_841":6424,"_809":6472},"https://github.com/gamedev-skills/awesome-gamedev-agent-skills","Godot · Unity · Unreal · Bevy · Phaser · PixiJS · Three.js · LÖVE · pygame · Roblox",[3533,1190,1650,1257,1376,6475],"Cline","Skills & instructions","skill",[706,694,696,702,695,6479],"cline","agent:playgama-web-game-assets-skill","playgama-web-game-assets-skill","Playgama: asset-production skill and GLB/audio build pipeline","A coding-agent skill for choosing a coherent asset set, recording credits, and preparing it for shipping. Its executable pipeline cleans and compresses GLB models while preserving names, handles audio conversion, and can re-encode textures.","/agents/playgama-web-game-assets-skill/",{"_804":6481,"_805":6482,"_802":6477,"_3":6516,"_920":6514,"_6434":6483,"_197":6513,"_6421":6510,"_6416":6507,"_6410":6503,"_6407":6502,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6517,"_6404":6501,"_6398":200},[6487,6488,6489,6490,6491,6492,6493,6494,6495,6496,6497,6498,6499,6500],{"_837":805,"_843":6482,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6483,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6476,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6515,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6514,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6511,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6508,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6505,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6504,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6503,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6502,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6501,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"Playgama","Requires Node 18+, glTF Transform, meshoptimizer, optional sharp, and ffmpeg for audio. Third-party components and assets are not bundled. This processes selected assets; it is not a generative-image/model service, a game engine, or a finished game.","SKILL.md plus scripts/assets.mjs. Verified the script’s geometry/texture/audio options, incremental hashing, name-preserving glTF processing, and CLI entry. Root installation matrix explicitly covers Gemini CLI, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and Copilot.","Mixed implementation and instructions",[6506],{"_841":6414,"_809":6507},"https://github.com/Playgama/gamedev-skills/blob/main/skills/web-game-assets/README.md",[6509],{"_841":6419,"_809":6510},"https://github.com/Playgama/gamedev-skills/tree/main/skills/web-game-assets",[6512],{"_841":6424,"_809":6513},"https://github.com/Playgama/gamedev-skills","Web games · glTF / GLB assets",[3533,1190,1650,1257,1376],[706,694,696,702,695],"mixed","agent:playgama-web-game-performance-skill","playgama-web-game-performance-skill","Playgama: web-game performance skill and executable probes","A reusable skill that measures a running game after warm-up and guides performance fixes using frame time, JavaScript cost, draw calls, and triangles. It includes both a headless measurement script and an in-game probe for real-device observation.","/agents/playgama-web-game-performance-skill/",{"_804":6519,"_805":6520,"_802":6477,"_3":6551,"_920":6549,"_6434":6521,"_197":6513,"_6421":6546,"_6416":6543,"_6410":6540,"_6407":6539,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6517,"_6404":6501,"_6398":200},[6525,6526,6527,6528,6529,6530,6531,6532,6533,6534,6535,6536,6537,6538],{"_837":805,"_843":6520,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6521,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6476,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6550,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6549,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6547,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6544,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6541,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6504,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6540,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6539,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6501,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"Needs Node 18+ and Puppeteer or puppeteer-core plus a Chrome executable. A throttled headless run is not a measurement of an actual phone; the author distinguishes comparable local runs from real-device telemetry. This is game-validation tooling, not a new game or a Google-authored extension.","SKILL.md plus scripts/perf.mjs and scripts/probe.js. Verified perf.mjs launches Puppeteer, accepts URL, warm-up/duration, phone emulation, readiness/setup hooks, JSON output, and before/after comparison. Root README explicitly documents Gemini CLI and the other named skill hosts.",[6542],{"_841":6414,"_809":6543},"https://github.com/Playgama/gamedev-skills/blob/main/skills/web-game-performance/README.md",[6545],{"_841":6419,"_809":6546},"https://github.com/Playgama/gamedev-skills/tree/main/skills/web-game-performance",[6548],{"_841":6424,"_809":6513},"Canvas / WebGL browser games",[3533,1190,1650,1257,1376],[706,694,696,702,695],"agent:godot-prompter-agent-skills","godot-prompter-agent-skills","GodotPrompter: multi-agent Godot skills and reusable movement code","A Godot-specific skill framework spanning gameplay, scene architecture, shaders, animation, testing, exports, and code review. It includes concrete GDScript/C# recipes, agent routing, platform-specific metadata, an OpenCode plugin, and machine-readable host verification status.","/agents/godot-prompter-agent-skills/",{"_804":6553,"_805":6554,"_802":6477,"_3":6588,"_920":6585,"_6434":6555,"_197":6584,"_6421":6581,"_6416":6578,"_6410":6575,"_6407":6574,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6517,"_6404":6573,"_6398":200},[6559,6560,6561,6562,6563,6564,6565,6566,6567,6568,6569,6570,6571,6572],{"_837":805,"_843":6554,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6555,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6476,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6586,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6585,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6582,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6579,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6576,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6504,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6575,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6574,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6573,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"jame581","The author marks Claude Code and Copilot CLI verified, Cursor registration as awaiting end-to-end confirmation, and several other hosts as documented only. Antigravity uses a documented GEMINI.md path; this is not presented as a verified Gemini CLI integration. Skills do not directly operate the Godot editor, and version-specific examples require matching the project’s Godot version.","Skills with implementation examples and host-integration code. Verified skills/player-controller/references/common-movement-recipes.md contains GDScript and C# dash/wall-jump recipes; .opencode/plugins/godot-prompter.js injects bootstrap context and registers skills; scripts/ validates skill/platform metadata. The repository uses master, not main.",[6577],{"_841":6414,"_809":6578},"https://github.com/jame581/GodotPrompter/blob/master/tests/agent-integration/host-smoke-matrix.json",[6580],{"_841":6419,"_809":6581},"https://github.com/jame581/GodotPrompter/tree/master/skills/player-controller",[6583],{"_841":6424,"_809":6584},"https://github.com/jame581/GodotPrompter","Godot 4.x · GDScript / C#",[2714,1190,1376,1257,1650,4698,6587],"Grok Build",[704,694,695,702,696,710,6589],"grok-build","agent:phaser-official-agent-skills","phaser-official-agent-skills","Phaser 4: official coding-agent skills with engine code examples","The Phaser engine repository now provides subsystem skills for agent-assisted development, including scenes, Arcade/Matter physics, input, assets, cameras, animation, UI, and migration. The official README explicitly names several coding agents, and the skills contain practical API examples linked to engine source.","/agents/phaser-official-agent-skills/",{"_804":6591,"_805":6592,"_802":6477,"_3":6625,"_920":6623,"_6434":6593,"_197":6622,"_6421":6619,"_6416":6616,"_6410":6613,"_6407":6612,"_6401":899,"_6413":6437,"_6404":6611,"_6398":200},[6597,6598,6599,6600,6601,6602,6603,6604,6605,6606,6607,6608,6609,6610],{"_837":805,"_843":6592,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6593,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6476,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6624,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6623,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6620,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6617,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6614,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6412,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6613,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6612,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6611,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6400,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"Phaser Studio","Targets Phaser 4; do not silently apply its rendering/migration guidance to Phaser 3 projects. A skill is knowledge and example code, not an editor-control service or a finished game. Agent names come from the official README and are not an end-to-end compatibility certification; Google models being mentioned is not treated as proof of Gemini CLI usage.","Reusable instruction files with JavaScript examples, backed by the engine implementation. Verified skills/physics-arcade/SKILL.md includes player/platform setup, collision registration, keyboard movement, and GameConfig; it points to src/physics/arcade/. Other exact paths include skills/scenes/SKILL.md and skills/v3-to-v4-migration/SKILL.md.",[6615],{"_841":6414,"_809":6616},"https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser/blob/master/skills/physics-arcade/SKILL.md",[6618],{"_841":6419,"_809":6619},"https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser/tree/master/skills",[6621],{"_841":6424,"_809":6622},"https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser#ai-assisted-game-development","Phaser 4 · JavaScript / TypeScript",[1190,1650,1257,2714,1376],[694,696,702,704,695],"agent:gemini-cli-godot-dock-bridge","gemini-cli-godot-dock-bridge","Gemini Assistant: a Godot dock backed by the actual Gemini CLI","A small community Godot editor plugin that sends prompts from a dock to a Python subprocess, invokes the installed gemini command, and handles returned file/folder creation instructions. Its code confirms a CLI integration rather than a direct Gemini API chat wrapper.","/agents/gemini-cli-godot-dock-bridge/",{"_804":6627,"_805":6628,"_802":6663,"_3":6664,"_920":6660,"_6434":6629,"_197":6659,"_6421":6656,"_6416":6653,"_6410":6649,"_6407":6648,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6647,"_6398":200},[6633,6634,6635,6636,6637,6638,6639,6640,6641,6642,6643,6644,6645,6646],{"_837":805,"_843":6628,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6629,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6661,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6660,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6657,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6654,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6651,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6649,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6648,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6647,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"AlexonMorris","Prototype bridge, not a complete game or full editor-control MCP server. Returned JSON file actions are applied automatically and existing files are opened in overwrite mode. The backend rejects '..' strings but does not enforce canonical project-root containment, so review it before use on valuable projects. It uses Windows type; macOS/Linux need the documented cat change. The dock expects python and addons/gemini_assistant/. Gemini CLI installation/authentication are separate prerequisites. No runtime validation was performed.","Editor-plugin source: gemini_plugin.gd registers the dock, gemini_dock.gd launches Python, and gemini_backend.py runs the gemini executable, parses JSON action blocks, and creates project files. Supporting dock scene and plugin configuration are in the repository.","Implementation",[6652],{"_841":6414,"_809":6653},"https://github.com/AlexonMorris/gemini_assistant_godot_plugin/blob/main/README.md",[6655],{"_841":6419,"_809":6656},"https://github.com/AlexonMorris/gemini_assistant_godot_plugin/blob/main/gemini_backend.py",[6658],{"_841":6424,"_809":6659},"https://github.com/AlexonMorris/gemini_assistant_godot_plugin","Godot 4 · GDScript · Python",[3533],"Engine bridges","bridge",[706],"implementation","agent:summer-gemini-engine-extension","summer-gemini-engine-extension","Summer: Gemini CLI extension, engine MCP, and game skills","A publisher-maintained CLI/MCP integration for building scenes, writing scripts, playing games, reading errors, and taking screenshots in Summer Engine. It includes a genuine Gemini extension manifest, context file, skill packaging, and cross-agent setup code.","/agents/summer-gemini-engine-extension/",{"_804":6667,"_805":6668,"_802":6663,"_3":6701,"_920":6699,"_6434":6669,"_197":6698,"_6421":6695,"_6416":6692,"_6410":6689,"_6407":6688,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6687,"_6398":200},[6673,6674,6675,6676,6677,6678,6679,6680,6681,6682,6683,6684,6685,6686],{"_837":805,"_843":6668,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6669,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6700,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6699,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6696,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6693,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6690,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6689,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6688,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6687,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"summerengine","Requires the separate Summer Engine desktop application for editor operations; the repository explicitly says it is not the engine itself. Hosted asset generation and publishing require a Summer account, and generation/paid builds consume credits. Gemini is a legacy setup target alongside current Antigravity guidance. No install or end-to-end compatibility test was performed here. This is not a Google-provided integration.","CLI/MCP integration source, not the engine source. Verified src/mcp/server.ts, src/cli/commands/setup.ts, src/installer/setup.ts, gemini-extension.json, integrations/gemini/README.md, scripts/build-gemini-extension.ts, and library/skills/. The Gemini packaging document explains the actual extension skills layout rather than assuming an arbitrary manifest skills key works.",[6691],{"_841":6414,"_809":6692},"https://github.com/summerengine/summer/blob/main/integrations/gemini/README.md",[6694],{"_841":6419,"_809":6695},"https://github.com/summerengine/summer/blob/main/src/mcp/server.ts",[6697],{"_841":6424,"_809":6698},"https://github.com/summerengine/summer","Summer Engine",[3533,2714,1650,1190,1257,1376,4698],[706,704,696,694,702,695,710],"agent:gamecraft-bench","gamecraft-bench","GameCraft-Bench","An end-to-end game-generation benchmark with 140 tasks across 15 families, runnable Godot workspaces, replayable input traces, screen recording, and hidden visual/gameplay rubrics.","/agents/gamecraft-bench/",{"_804":6703,"_805":6704,"_802":6739,"_3":6740,"_920":6735,"_6434":6705,"_197":6734,"_6421":6731,"_6416":6728,"_6410":6725,"_6407":6724,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6723,"_6398":200},[6709,6710,6711,6712,6713,6714,6715,6716,6717,6718,6719,6720,6721,6722],{"_837":805,"_843":6704,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6705,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6738,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6736,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6735,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6732,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6729,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6726,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6725,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6724,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6723,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"FreedomIntelligence","Godot 4.6.2 and Linux/Xvfb/input-recording dependencies are pinned in the reproduction guide. Expected asset libraries are downloaded separately, with per-entry licensing. Rubric scores depend on the judge and replay protocol; Gemini judge support is not evidence of a Gemini CLI coding-agent adapter.","Verified local Harbor agent/environment code, replay and scoring implementations, model-judge adapters, wrapper scripts for Claude Code/Codex/Kimi Code, and committed task instructions/reference-solution GDScript. The author's project site links this repository directly.",[6727],{"_841":6414,"_809":6728},"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/blob/main/README.md",[6730],{"_841":6419,"_809":6731},"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench/tree/main/gamecraft_bench",[6733],{"_841":6424,"_809":6734},"https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/gamecraft-bench","Godot",[1190,1650,6737],"Kimi Code","Development evaluations","evaluation",[694,696,6741],"kimi-code","agent:gamelogicbench","gamelogicbench","GameLogicBench","A coding-agent benchmark of 72 gameplay-logic tasks whose deterministic Godot evaluators check observable state at each simulation tick rather than grading agent-written claims.","/agents/gamelogicbench/",{"_804":6743,"_805":6744,"_802":6739,"_3":6776,"_920":6735,"_6434":6745,"_197":6774,"_6421":6771,"_6416":6768,"_6410":6765,"_6407":6764,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6763,"_6398":200},[6749,6750,6751,6752,6753,6754,6755,6756,6757,6758,6759,6760,6761,6762],{"_837":805,"_843":6744,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6745,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6738,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6775,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6735,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6772,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6769,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6766,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6765,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6764,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6763,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"NJU-LINK","Requires Docker, a matching Godot 4.4 environment, an agent CLI package, task-library checkout, and configured model endpoints. It evaluates runtime game logic, not visual quality or finished commercial-game production. Network restrictions and task-library commit materially affect results; do not treat model backends as additional coding-agent adapters.","Verified Python solve/judge/record pipeline, container/egress code, and separate claude_code.py, codex.py, and opencode.py adapters. The public GameLogicBench-Tasks repository is a separate dependency and contains the game/task/judge/reference content.",[6767],{"_841":6414,"_809":6768},"https://github.com/NJU-LINK/GameLogicBench/blob/main/docs/running.md",[6770],{"_841":6419,"_809":6771},"https://github.com/NJU-LINK/GameLogicBench/tree/main/geb",[6773],{"_841":6424,"_809":6774},"https://github.com/NJU-LINK/GameLogicBench",[1190,1650,4698],[694,696,710],"agent:unreal-mcp-codex-runners","unreal-mcp-codex-runners","Unreal Engine MCP for Codex · Community Skill and Runners","A community Codex adaptation of Epic's Unreal MCP workflow, with concrete command-line helpers for environment probes, automation tests, Python commandlets, builds, and smoke cooks.","/agents/unreal-mcp-codex-runners/",{"_804":6778,"_805":6779,"_802":6435,"_3":6812,"_920":6810,"_6434":6780,"_197":6809,"_6421":6806,"_6416":6803,"_6410":6800,"_6407":6799,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6517,"_6404":6798,"_6398":200},[6784,6785,6786,6787,6788,6789,6790,6791,6792,6793,6794,6795,6796,6797],{"_837":805,"_843":6779,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6780,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6433,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6811,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6810,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6807,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6804,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6801,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6504,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6800,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6799,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6798,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"WildCake","Documents Unreal 5.8+ native MCP and requires a separately installed engine/toolsets. Several runners and examples are Windows-oriented; Codex integration is community-maintained, not endorsed by Epic or OpenAI. It does not bundle the engine server or a complete game.","Verified actual Python implementations: check_unreal_mcp.py, run_unreal_automation.py, run_unreal_python.py, build_unreal.py, cook_unreal.py, shared process/log helpers, plus a PowerShell probe and Codex plugin/config metadata.",[6802],{"_841":6414,"_809":6803},"https://github.com/WildCake/unreal-engine-mcp-codex#headless-runners",[6805],{"_841":6419,"_809":6806},"https://github.com/WildCake/unreal-engine-mcp-codex/tree/main/skills/unreal-engine-mcp-codex/scripts",[6808],{"_841":6424,"_809":6809},"https://github.com/WildCake/unreal-engine-mcp-codex","Unreal Engine",[1650],[696],"agent:unity-agent-workflow-skills","unity-agent-workflow-skills","Unity Agent · CLI, Headless, MCP, and Package Skills","A reusable Unity workflow pack that routes agent work through CLI probes, batchmode validation, MCP selection, package management, and evidence-based completion checks.","/agents/unity-agent-workflow-skills/",{"_804":6814,"_805":6815,"_802":6477,"_3":6848,"_920":6846,"_6434":6816,"_197":6845,"_6421":6842,"_6416":6839,"_6410":6836,"_6407":6835,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6517,"_6404":6834,"_6398":200},[6820,6821,6822,6823,6824,6825,6826,6827,6828,6829,6830,6831,6832,6833],{"_837":805,"_843":6815,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6816,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6476,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6847,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6846,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6843,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6840,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6837,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6504,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6836,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6835,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6834,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"m4bwav","The included deterministic probes/runners are PowerShell-oriented. Unity, its CLI/Pipeline package, SDKs, and chosen MCP bridge are separate dependencies; the skill pack installs none of them. Cross-agent support means documented instruction discovery, not identical end-to-end validation on all listed clients.","Verified five SKILL.md workflows, executable unity_probe.ps1 and unity_headless.ps1 JSON-output wrappers, and PackageInstaller.cs. The README explicitly lists cross-agent skill consumption; these are community procedures around Unity tools, not the Unity CLI implementation.",[6838],{"_841":6414,"_809":6839},"https://github.com/m4bwav/unity-agent/blob/master/README.md",[6841],{"_841":6419,"_809":6842},"https://github.com/m4bwav/unity-agent/tree/master/skills",[6844],{"_841":6424,"_809":6845},"https://github.com/m4bwav/unity-agent","Unity",[1190,1650,3533,1257,1376],[694,696,706,702,695],"agent:agent2unity-cli","agent2unity-cli","A .NET command-line client plus a C# Unity editor daemon that lets coding agents create and modify Unity assets through editor APIs and run compilation/test checks.","/agents/agent2unity-cli/",{"_804":6850,"_805":6850,"_802":6663,"_3":6882,"_920":6846,"_6434":6851,"_197":6880,"_6421":6877,"_6416":6874,"_6410":6871,"_6407":6870,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6869,"_6398":200},[6855,6856,6857,6858,6859,6860,6861,6862,6863,6864,6865,6866,6867,6868],{"_837":805,"_843":6850,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6851,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6881,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6846,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6878,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6875,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6872,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6871,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6870,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6869,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"jkpp","Requires a running Unity Editor/daemon and .NET SDK 8; tests additionally need Unity Test Framework. The daemon binds to localhost but has no authentication check in the reviewed request path, so any process that can reach the port can invoke editor commands. Keep it local and stop it when unused. It controls documented editor operations, not arbitrary gameplay acceptance; agent instruction files do not establish equal live testing.","Verified .NET CLI Program.cs, C# HTTP daemon/main-thread dispatcher, serialized-field and prefab/scene commands, and Unity Test Framework command implementations. Agent integration files explicitly cover Claude Code skills, Codex AGENTS.md, Cursor rules, and Gemini CLI GEMINI.md.",[6873],{"_841":6414,"_809":6874},"https://github.com/jkpp/agent2unity-cli/tree/main/agents",[6876],{"_841":6419,"_809":6877},"https://github.com/jkpp/agent2unity-cli/tree/main/unity-plugin/Agent2Unity/Editor",[6879],{"_841":6424,"_809":6880},"https://github.com/jkpp/agent2unity-cli",[1190,1650,1257,3533],[694,696,702,706],"agent:godot-agent-loop","godot-agent-loop","Godot Agent Loop","A Godot build–run–observe–playtest–verify loop with runtime/editor bridge code, reusable skills, and retained execution evidence.","/agents/godot-agent-loop/",{"_804":6884,"_805":6885,"_802":6919,"_3":6920,"_920":6735,"_6434":6886,"_197":6915,"_6421":6912,"_6416":6909,"_6410":6906,"_6407":6905,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6517,"_6404":6904,"_6398":200},[6890,6891,6892,6893,6894,6895,6896,6897,6898,6899,6900,6901,6902,6903],{"_837":805,"_843":6885,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6886,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6918,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6916,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6735,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6913,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6910,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6907,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6504,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6906,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6905,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6904,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"beremaran","Requires Godot 4.7+ and Node 22+. The default core tool surface uses godot_catalog and godot_call to reach unlisted tools. Filesystem access is denied without configured roots unless explicitly overridden; runtime reflection and code-execution groups are disabled by default. Those RPC gates do not sandbox project GDScript, which runs with OS-level permissions. Screenshots need a rendering/display context. Linux CI, Windows acceptance, and specific macOS workflows are reported separately, not as equal coverage across clients and platforms.","Verified TypeScript server/editor bridge, addons/godot_agent_loop/plugin.gd, runtime verification code, cold-model evaluation runners, and an executable launch-demo project. One portable agent bundle exposes build/debug/verify/ship skills and explicit Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Pi adapters.",[6908],{"_841":6414,"_809":6909},"https://github.com/beremaran/godot-agent-loop/blob/main/docs/agent-plugin.md",[6911],{"_841":6419,"_809":6912},"https://github.com/beremaran/godot-agent-loop/tree/main/src",[6914],{"_841":6424,"_809":6915},"https://github.com/beremaran/godot-agent-loop",[1190,1650,4698,6917],"Pi","Development frameworks","framework",[694,696,710,6921],"pi","agent:gda-godot-agent","gda-godot-agent","gda · Godot Automation for AI Agents","A CLI, reusable skill, and MCP surface for editing Godot content, validating projects, and collecting runtime tree, input, screenshots, logs, and performance evidence.","/agents/gda-godot-agent/",{"_804":6923,"_805":6924,"_802":6663,"_3":6956,"_920":6735,"_6434":6925,"_197":6954,"_6421":6951,"_6416":6948,"_6410":6945,"_6407":6944,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6943,"_6398":200},[6929,6930,6931,6932,6933,6934,6935,6936,6937,6938,6939,6940,6941,6942],{"_837":805,"_843":6924,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6925,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6955,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6735,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6952,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6949,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6946,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6945,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6944,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6943,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"aigengame","Requires Python 3.13+ and Godot 4.4+ for headless operations or 4.6+ for Live. It assumes a trusted project: even some read-only operations start autoloads, and node get instantiates scene scripts. Runtime screenshots need a windowed/display session. Live mode injects a development harness; exports must respect its stripping/self-disable behavior. Other MCP clients are not individually verified here.","Verified Python CLI/MCP implementation under src/gda, daemon IPC, and an actual GDScript runtime harness at src/gda/harness/gda_harness.gd. skills/gda/SKILL.md and docs/gda-skill.md provide agent guidance; documented configuration explicitly covers Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor.",[6947],{"_841":6414,"_809":6948},"https://github.com/aigengame/godot-agent#register-with-coding-agents",[6950],{"_841":6419,"_809":6951},"https://github.com/aigengame/godot-agent/tree/main/src/gda",[6953],{"_841":6424,"_809":6954},"https://github.com/aigengame/godot-agent",[1190,1650,1257],[694,696,702],"agent:godot-cli-live-editor","godot-cli-live-editor","Godot CLI · live scene authoring for coding agents","A Go command-line client and embedded Godot editor bridge that let coding agents write scripts, construct scenes, connect signals, run checks, and inspect runtime screenshots.","/agents/godot-cli-live-editor/",{"_804":6958,"_805":6959,"_802":6663,"_3":6992,"_920":6990,"_6434":6960,"_197":6989,"_6421":6986,"_6416":6983,"_6410":6980,"_6407":6979,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":6978,"_6398":200},[6964,6965,6966,6967,6968,6969,6970,6971,6972,6973,6974,6975,6976,6977],{"_837":805,"_843":6959,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6960,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":6991,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":6990,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":6987,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":6984,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":6981,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":6980,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":6979,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":6978,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"trunglqdev","Requires Godot plus the editor daemon for live authoring; source builds require Go. The bridge owns an active scene that must be opened/created and saved explicitly in headless mode. It is an independent community CLI, not Godot's official command-line interface.","Reviewed the Go stdio MCP wrapper and the GDScript EditorPlugin's JSON-RPC dispatch and scene operations. The CLI exposes the command surface to MCP clients while Claude Code can call it through a shell; 2D and 3D acceptance game source is included.",[6982],{"_841":6414,"_809":6983},"https://github.com/trunglqdev/Godot_CLI/blob/2e8f8636ae6c5f75071a4968df114186eacad40a/mcp.go",[6985],{"_841":6419,"_809":6986},"https://github.com/trunglqdev/Godot_CLI/blob/2e8f8636ae6c5f75071a4968df114186eacad40a/addon/godot_cli_bridge/plugin.gd",[6988],{"_841":6424,"_809":6989},"https://github.com/trunglqdev/Godot_CLI","Godot 4 / GDScript / Go CLI",[1190,1257,4440],[694,702,709],"agent:godot-forge-code-quality","godot-forge-code-quality","Godot Forge · code analysis and tests (gregario)","A focused MCP feedback layer for coding agents: Godot API lookup, GDScript and scene checks, actual editor diagnostics, and structured GUT/GdUnit4 test results.","/agents/godot-forge-code-quality/",{"_804":6994,"_805":6995,"_802":6663,"_3":7028,"_920":7026,"_6434":6996,"_197":7025,"_6421":7022,"_6416":7019,"_6410":7016,"_6407":7015,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":7014,"_6398":200},[7000,7001,7002,7003,7004,7005,7006,7007,7008,7009,7010,7011,7012,7013],{"_837":805,"_843":6995,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":6996,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":7027,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":7026,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":7023,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":7020,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":7017,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":7016,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":7015,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":7014,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"gregario","Heuristic warnings differ from compiler diagnostics. Tests need Godot plus GUT/GdUnit4. At the cited source revision, static source inspection indicates that unrecognized output can produce 'All 0 tests passed' and the result does not incorporate the process exit code. This failure path was not runtime-reproduced; verify expected counts and raw execution evidence before accepting a pass. LSP diagnostics need the editor; screenshots launch a separate Godot process and need a display. It is a feedback layer, not broad scene authoring.","Reviewed MCP test registration, Godot process launch and GUT/GdUnit4 output parsers; also reviewed heuristic script analysis and an LSP client that obtains editor diagnostics. Scene analysis, project launching and screenshots have separate modules.",[7018],{"_841":6414,"_809":7019},"https://github.com/gregario/godot-forge/blob/401f41494eb0777c1e5c848e0e7cce5cafd9cc25/src/tools/script-analysis.ts",[7021],{"_841":6419,"_809":7022},"https://github.com/gregario/godot-forge/blob/401f41494eb0777c1e5c848e0e7cce5cafd9cc25/src/tools/test-runner.ts",[7024],{"_841":6424,"_809":7025},"https://github.com/gregario/godot-forge","Godot 4 / GDScript",[1190,1650,3533,1257],[694,696,706,702],"agent:godot-forge-editor-bridge","godot-forge-editor-bridge","Godot Forge · live editor and runtime bridge (Tann2019)","An MCP server and Godot add-on for writing scripts, building editable scenes, reading diagnostics, running games, simulating input, and checking mechanics with saved scenarios.","/agents/godot-forge-editor-bridge/",{"_804":7030,"_805":7031,"_802":6663,"_3":7063,"_920":7026,"_6434":7032,"_197":7061,"_6421":7058,"_6416":7055,"_6410":7052,"_6407":7051,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":7050,"_6398":200},[7036,7037,7038,7039,7040,7041,7042,7043,7044,7045,7046,7047,7048,7049],{"_837":805,"_843":7031,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":7032,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":7062,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":7026,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":7059,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":7056,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":7053,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":7052,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":7051,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":7050,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"Tann2019","Requires Godot 4.4+ and Node 20+. Live authoring uses the editor add-on; runtime inspection and input need a running game with the debugger connection. Documentation, tests, and export also have separate headless paths. Code review confirms implemented paths, not successful execution of every operation. This is separate from Coding-Solo/godot-mcp and gregario/godot-forge.","Reviewed script creation/edit/validation/attachment handlers, the runtime command forwarder, and the companion skill. The tree includes a TypeScript MCP bridge, GDScript editor/runtime handlers, and a platformer with a coin-collection test scenario.",[7054],{"_841":6414,"_809":7055},"https://github.com/Tann2019/godot-mcp-server/blob/b0da85fac67dd067c16bfe791227c0e7edb56d7e/skills/godot-forge/SKILL.md",[7057],{"_841":6419,"_809":7058},"https://github.com/Tann2019/godot-mcp-server/blob/b0da85fac67dd067c16bfe791227c0e7edb56d7e/addons/godot_forge/handlers/script.gd",[7060],{"_841":6424,"_809":7061},"https://github.com/Tann2019/godot-mcp-server",[1190,1650,1257],[694,696,702],"agent:ione-unity-claude","ione-unity-claude","ione · Unity HTTP bridge and Claude Code skill","Connects Claude Code to Unity through an opt-in local HTTP bridge so the agent can inspect scenes, create C# scripts, wait for compilation, and verify the game view.","/agents/ione-unity-claude/",{"_804":7065,"_805":7066,"_802":6663,"_3":7099,"_920":7097,"_6434":7067,"_197":7096,"_6421":7093,"_6416":7090,"_6410":7087,"_6407":7086,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":7085,"_6398":200},[7071,7072,7073,7074,7075,7076,7077,7078,7079,7080,7081,7082,7083,7084],{"_837":805,"_843":7066,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":7067,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6662,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":7098,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":7097,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":7094,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":7091,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":7088,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":7087,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":7086,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":7085,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"TestcodeInc","Requires Unity 2022.3+ and the opt-in, bearer-authenticated local bridge. Script writes, asset deletion, menu execution, Play Mode, and scene switching are permitted by default unless disabled in Settings. Unity Undo does not cover file writes or most AssetDatabase operations. Domain reload temporarily interrupts the listener, and Unity must service its main thread. The Claude Code bridge needs no separate provider API key; in-editor chat and image generation have separate API requirements.","Reviewed the exact Claude skill, loopback HttpListener implementation, and AssetTools.CreateScript. The skill calls the bridge's live schema, follows script writes with wait_for_compile, and checks capture_game_view.",[7089],{"_841":6414,"_809":7090},"https://github.com/TestcodeInc/ione/blob/5c668fb32efa7e832ce932f0536980b22808e3df/ClaudeSkill/SKILL.md",[7092],{"_841":6419,"_809":7093},"https://github.com/TestcodeInc/ione/blob/5c668fb32efa7e832ce932f0536980b22808e3df/Editor/Core/IoneHttpBridge.cs",[7095],{"_841":6424,"_809":7096},"https://github.com/TestcodeInc/ione","Unity / C#",[1190],[694],"agent:tea-leaves-game-harness","tea-leaves-game-harness","Tea Leaves · Claude Code Godot verification harness","A reusable Godot project substrate that gives Claude Code runtime state, screenshots, simulated input, scene validation, and tests while it writes and repairs game code.","/agents/tea-leaves-game-harness/",{"_804":7101,"_805":7102,"_802":6919,"_3":7135,"_920":7133,"_6434":7103,"_197":7132,"_6421":7129,"_6416":7126,"_6410":7123,"_6407":7122,"_6401":2869,"_6413":6665,"_6404":7121,"_6398":200},[7107,7108,7109,7110,7111,7112,7113,7114,7115,7116,7117,7118,7119,7120],{"_837":805,"_843":7102,"_839":805,"_858":-7},{"_837":921,"_843":7103,"_839":6434,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6432,"_843":6918,"_839":802,"_858":909},{"_837":849,"_841":6430,"_898":2869,"_851":7134,"_839":3,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6428,"_843":7133,"_839":920,"_858":909},{"_837":854,"_841":6424,"_851":7130,"_839":197,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6419,"_851":7127,"_839":6421,"_858":-7},{"_837":854,"_841":6414,"_851":7124,"_839":6416,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6411,"_843":6650,"_839":6413,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6408,"_843":7123,"_839":6410,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6405,"_843":7122,"_839":6407,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6402,"_843":7121,"_839":6404,"_858":909},{"_837":838,"_841":6399,"_843":6460,"_839":6401,"_858":-7},{"_837":838,"_841":6397,"_843":200,"_839":6398,"_858":917},"cleak","A project-specific substrate rather than a universal Godot editor bridge. Defaults assume a Windows-oriented Godot Mono toolchain and include a hard-coded monitor selection; paths and window settings need adaptation. No installation or execution was performed.","Reviewed the C# DevTools autoload, Python CLI, and Claude project guide. Actual code dispatches screenshot/scene-tree/state commands and asynchronous input sequences; companion validators, shader lint and test wrappers are present.",[7125],{"_841":6414,"_809":7126},"https://github.com/cleak/tea-leaves/blob/b465c6bdf2c283a16eaa805c5f5f4f21c1f05cc8/CLAUDE.md",[7128],{"_841":6419,"_809":7129},"https://github.com/cleak/tea-leaves/blob/b465c6bdf2c283a16eaa805c5f5f4f21c1f05cc8/game/DevTools.cs",[7131],{"_841":6424,"_809":7132},"https://github.com/cleak/tea-leaves","Godot 4.6 Mono / C# / .NET 8",[1